window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b004-ebe37b78fdeb52be.json"]={sha256:"ebe37b78fdeb52be99f0d5c5cdfad2fb5434b9ada42023f7b45a7760af7e93b0",value:{"id":"b004","title":"1915 恰納卡萊大橋","titleEn":"1915 Canakkale Bridge","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"1915 恰納卡萊大橋以 2,023 m 主跨橫跨達達尼爾海峽，2022 年通車，鋼塔高 318 m。本課從垂跨比與塔高的取捨出發，計算 1,960 MPa 級平行鋼絲主纜的斷面，說明在地震帶海床上以乾塢預製、拖航沉放的沉箱作為隔震式基礎，再處理索鞍預偏、87 個橋面節塊吊裝、雙箱梁風洞試驗、吊索力量測、鋼橋面疲勞與伸縮縫交接。","summaryEn":"The 1915 Çanakkale Bridge crosses the Dardanelles with a 2,023 m main span and 318 m steel towers, opening in 2022. The course starts from the trade-off between sag ratio and tower height, sizes a parallel-wire cable of 1,960 MPa class wire, explains caissons built in dry dock, towed and set on a seismic seabed as an isolated foundation, then covers saddle presetting, lifting 87 deck blocks, twin-box wind-tunnel testing, hanger-force measurement, steel-deck fatigue and expansion-joint handover.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-suspension","subcategoryTitle":"懸索橋巨作與主纜系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Suspension bridges and main-cable systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-suspension","learningTags":["structures","st-suspension","suspension"],"architectureFamily":"suspension","architectureNodes":[["318 m 鋼塔與索鞍","318 m steel towers and saddles"],["1,960 MPa 主纜","1,960 MPa main cables"],["吊索","Hangers"],["雙箱鋼橋面","Twin-box steel deck"],["隔震式沉箱與錨碇","Isolated caissons and anchorages"],["伸縮縫與監測","Expansion joints and monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[1,0],[0,4],[1,4],[3,5]],"diagram":{"type":"suspension","labels":["318 m 鋼塔與索鞍","1,960 MPa 主纜","吊索","雙箱鋼橋面","隔震式沉箱與錨碇"],"labelsEn":["318 m steel towers and saddles","1,960 MPa main cables","Hangers","Twin-box steel deck","Isolated caissons and anchorages"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：主跨 l = 2,023 m，每條主纜承受恆載 w = 137.3 kN/m（兩纜合計 28 t/m），主纜鋼絲面積 A = 0.4749 m²，鋼絲強度 1,960 MPa。方案甲垂跨比 1/8.5：f = 238.0 m，H = w·l²/(8f) = 137.3×2,023²/(8×238.0) ≈ 295 MN，塔頂張力 T = H·√(1+16n²) ≈ 295×1.105 ≈ 326 MN，應力 326/0.4749 ≈ 687 MPa，恆載安全係數約 2.85，塔高約 317 m。方案乙垂跨比 1/10：f = 202.3 m，H ≈ 347 MN，T ≈ 374 MN，應力約 788 MPa，係數約 2.49，塔高約 281 m。降低塔高約 36 m 的代價是主纜張力增加約 15%，若要維持相同安全係數，鋼絲面積須增加約 15%，自重再推高張力。數值為教學假設，不代表 1915 恰納卡萊大橋的設計計算。","textEn":"Design exercise: main span l = 2,023 m, dead load per cable w = 137.3 kN/m (28 t/m for both cables), wire area per cable A = 0.4749 m², wire strength 1,960 MPa. Option A, sag ratio 1/8.5: f = 238.0 m, H = w·l²/(8f) = 137.3×2,023²/(8×238.0) ≈ 295 MN, tower-top tension T = H·√(1+16n²) ≈ 295×1.105 ≈ 326 MN, stress 326/0.4749 ≈ 687 MPa, dead-load safety factor about 2.85, tower about 317 m. Option B, sag ratio 1/10: f = 202.3 m, H ≈ 347 MN, T ≈ 374 MN, stress about 788 MPa, factor about 2.49, tower about 281 m. Cutting about 36 m of tower height costs about 15% more cable tension; keeping the same safety factor needs about 15% more wire, whose weight pushes tension up again. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design calculations of the 1915 Çanakkale Bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b004-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨」與「寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Main span, sag ratio and tower height\" and \"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b004-v13-01","title":"主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Main span, sag ratio and tower height: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sag ratio and 318 m towers” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"懸索橋的主纜幾何由三個數字綁在一起：主跨、垂度與航道淨空。業主公開的配置為 770 m + 2,023 m + 770 m，鋼塔高 318 m（含頂部砲彈造型裝飾為 334 m），垂直航行淨空 70 m、水平航行淨空 1,600 m。垂度越大，主纜水平張力越小、鋼絲用量越省，但塔必須更高、塔與基礎承受更大的彎矩與風載；垂度越小則塔較矮但主纜更重。2,023 m 這個數字具有建國百年的象徵意義，工程團隊需要在此限制下用垂跨比平衡塔高與纜索張力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The main-cable geometry of a suspension bridge ties three numbers together: main span, sag and navigation clearance. The owner's published layout is 770 m + 2,023 m + 770 m, with 318 m steel towers (334 m including the shell-shaped finials), 70 m vertical and 1,600 m horizontal navigation clearance. More sag lowers horizontal cable tension and saves wire, but the towers must be taller and the towers and foundations carry larger moments and wind loads; less sag gives shorter towers but heavier cables. The 2,023 m figure carries the symbolism of the Republic's centenary, so the team had to balance tower height and cable tension through the sag ratio within that constraint. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Sag ratio and 318 m towers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：塔頂高程 ≈ 跨中橋面高程 + 纜梁最小間距 + 垂度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Tower-top level ≈ mid-span deck level + minimum cable-to-girder gap + sag.","failure":"常見誤解：「塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Sag ratio and 318 m towers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-01-k1","title":"主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨","titleEn":"Main span, sag ratio and tower height","text":"懸索橋的主纜幾何由三個數字綁在一起：主跨、垂度與航道淨空。業主公開的配置為 770 m + 2,023 m + 770 m，鋼塔高 318 m（含頂部砲彈造型裝飾為 334 m），垂直航行淨空 70 m、水平航行淨空 1,600 m。","textEn":"The main-cable geometry of a suspension bridge ties three numbers together: main span, sag and navigation clearance. The owner's published layout is 770 m + 2,023 m + 770 m, with 318 m steel towers (334 m including the shell-shaped finials), 70 m vertical and 1,600 m horizontal navigation clearance.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Main span, sag ratio and tower height\" is correct?","options":["塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。","懸索橋的主纜幾何由三個數字綁在一起：主跨、垂度與航道淨空。","橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。"],"optionsEn":["Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper.","The main-cable geometry of a suspension bridge ties three numbers together: main span, sag and navigation clearance.","An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"懸索橋的主纜幾何由三個數字綁在一起：主跨、垂度與航道淨空。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The main-cable geometry of a suspension bridge ties three numbers together: main span, sag and navigation clearance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b004-v13-02","title":"主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨：定量估算","titleEn":"Main span, sag ratio and tower height: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sag ratio and 318 m towers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：塔頂高程 ≈ 跨中橋面高程 + 纜梁最小間距 + 垂度。取橋面 72.8 m、間距 6 m、垂跨比 1/8.5：f = 2,023/8.5 = 238.0 m，塔高約 72.8 + 6 + 238 ≈ 317 m；若改為 1/10，f = 202.3 m，塔高約 281 m，但水平張力 H ∝ 1/n 增加 18%。間距與垂跨比為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Tower-top level ≈ mid-span deck level + minimum cable-to-girder gap + sag. With the deck at 72.8 m, a 6 m gap and sag ratio 1/8.5: f = 2,023/8.5 = 238.0 m and the tower is about 72.8 + 6 + 238 ≈ 317 m; at 1/10, f = 202.3 m and the tower is about 281 m, but horizontal tension H ∝ 1/n rises 18%. Gap and sag ratio are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以參數研究比較不同垂跨比下的主纜鋼量、塔鋼量、基礎反力與塔頂風致位移，畫出總造價或總鋼量對垂跨比的曲線；配置定案後，以航道主管機關核准的淨空包絡線檢查最不利溫度與活載下的橋面最低點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run a parametric study comparing cable steel, tower steel, foundation reactions and wind-induced tower-top displacement for several sag ratios, plotting total cost or steel against sag ratio; once fixed, check the lowest deck point under the worst temperature and live load against the clearance envelope approved by the navigation authority.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"塔頂高程 ≈ 跨中橋面高程 + 纜梁最小間距 + 垂度。取橋面 72.8 m、間距 6 m、垂跨比 1/8.5：f = 2,023/8.5 = 238.0 m，塔高約 72.8 + 6 + 238 ≈ 317 m；若改為 1/10，f = 202.3 m，塔高約 281 m，但水平張力 H ∝ 1/n 增加 18%。間距與垂跨比為教學假設。","textEn":"Tower-top level ≈ mid-span deck level + minimum cable-to-girder gap + sag. With the deck at 72.8 m, a 6 m gap and sag ratio 1/8.5: f = 2,023/8.5 = 238.0 m and the tower is about 72.8 + 6 + 238 ≈ 317 m; at 1/10, f = 202.3 m and the tower is about 281 m, but horizontal tension H ∝ 1/n rises 18%. Gap and sag ratio are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Main span, sag ratio and tower height\", which statement holds?","options":["基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。","索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","塔頂高程 ≈ 跨中橋面高程 + 纜梁最小間距 + 垂度。"],"optionsEn":["If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed.","Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","Tower-top level ≈ mid-span deck level + minimum cable-to-girder gap + sag."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塔頂高程 ≈ 跨中橋面高程 + 纜梁最小間距 + 垂度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Tower-top level ≈ mid-span deck level + minimum cable-to-girder gap + sag. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b004-v13-03","title":"主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Main span, sag ratio and tower height: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sag ratio and 318 m towers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以參數研究比較不同垂跨比下的主纜鋼量、塔鋼量、基礎反力與塔頂風致位移，畫出總造價或總鋼量對垂跨比的曲線；配置定案後，以航道主管機關核准的淨空包絡線檢查最不利溫度與活載下的橋面最低點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run a parametric study comparing cable steel, tower steel, foundation reactions and wind-induced tower-top displacement for several sag ratios, plotting total cost or steel against sag ratio; once fixed, check the lowest deck point under the worst temperature and live load against the clearance envelope approved by the navigation authority. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：總體配置階段應保存垂跨比比較表與航道淨空核准文件，並把選定的垂跨比、塔高與溫度假設寫入設計基準書，日後任何線形變更都要回到此基準重新檢核淨空與張力。","observationEn":"Site practice: At the general-arrangement stage keep the sag-ratio comparison table and the navigation clearance approval, and write the chosen sag ratio, tower height and temperature assumptions into the design basis, so any later profile change is re-checked against clearance and tension from that baseline.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以主纜鋼量最省選擇大垂度，塔高與塔底彎矩可能增加到基礎難以承受，也延長塔施工與高空作業時間；反之垂度過小，主纜張力與錨碇規模暴增，錨碇基礎可能成為控制造價的瓶頸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Choosing a large sag only to minimise cable steel can raise tower height and base moment beyond what the foundations can comfortably take and lengthen high-level tower work; too little sag inflates cable tension and anchorage size, making anchorage foundations the cost bottleneck. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以參數研究比較不同垂跨比下的主纜鋼量、塔鋼量、基礎反力與塔頂風致位移，畫出總造價或總鋼量對垂跨比的曲線；配置定案後，以航道主管機關核准的淨空包絡線檢查最不利溫度與活載下的橋面最低點。","textEn":"Run a parametric study comparing cable steel, tower steel, foundation reactions and wind-induced tower-top displacement for several sag ratios, plotting total cost or steel against sag ratio; once fixed, check the lowest deck point under the worst temperature and live load against the clearance envelope approved by the navigation authority.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"總體配置階段應保存垂跨比比較表與航道淨空核准文件，並把選定的垂跨比、塔高與溫度假設寫入設計基準書，日後任何線形變更都要回到此基準重新檢核淨空與張力。","textEn":"At the general-arrangement stage keep the sag-ratio comparison table and the navigation clearance approval, and write the chosen sag ratio, tower height and temperature assumptions into the design basis, so any later profile change is re-checked against clearance and tension from that baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Main span, sag ratio and tower height\"?","options":["以參數研究比較不同垂跨比下的主纜鋼量、塔鋼量、基礎反力與塔頂風致位移，畫出總造價或總鋼量對垂跨比的曲線。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。"],"optionsEn":["Run a parametric study comparing cable steel, tower steel, foundation reactions and wind-induced tower-top displacement for several sag ratios, plotting total cost or steel against sag ratio.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以參數研究比較不同垂跨比下的主纜鋼量、塔鋼量、基礎反力與塔頂風致位移，畫出總造價或總鋼量對垂跨比的曲線；配置定案後，以航道主管機關核准的淨空包絡線檢查最不利溫度與活載下的橋面最低點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run a parametric study comparing cable steel, tower steel, foundation reactions and wind-induced tower-top displacement for several sag ratios, plotting total cost or steel against sag ratio; once fixed, check the lowest deck point under the worst temperature and live load against the clearance envelope approved by the navigation authority. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b004-v13-04","title":"主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨：失效診斷","titleEn":"Main span, sag ratio and tower height: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂跨比與 318 m 塔高」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sag ratio and 318 m towers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以主纜鋼量最省選擇大垂度，塔高與塔底彎矩可能增加到基礎難以承受，也延長塔施工與高空作業時間；反之垂度過小，主纜張力與錨碇規模暴增，錨碇基礎可能成為控制造價的瓶頸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Choosing a large sag only to minimise cable steel can raise tower height and base moment beyond what the foundations can comfortably take and lengthen high-level tower work; too little sag inflates cable tension and anchorage size, making anchorage foundations the cost bottleneck. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：2,023 m 這個數字具有建國百年的象徵意義，工程團隊需要在此限制下用垂跨比平衡塔高與纜索張力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The 2,023 m figure carries the symbolism of the Republic's centenary, so the team had to balance tower height and cable tension through the sag ratio within that constraint.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以主纜鋼量最省選擇大垂度，塔高與塔底彎矩可能增加到基礎難以承受，也延長塔施工與高空作業時間；反之垂度過小，主纜張力與錨碇規模暴增，錨碇基礎可能成為控制造價的瓶頸。","textEn":"Choosing a large sag only to minimise cable steel can raise tower height and base moment beyond what the foundations can comfortably take and lengthen high-level tower work; too little sag inflates cable tension and anchorage size, making anchorage foundations the cost bottleneck.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主跨、垂跨比與塔高的取捨」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Main span, sag ratio and tower height\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只以主纜鋼量最省選擇大垂度，塔高與塔底彎矩可能增加到基礎難以承受，也延長塔施工與高空作業時間。","橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Choosing a large sag only to minimise cable steel can raise tower height and base moment beyond what the foundations can comfortably take and lengthen high-level tower work.","An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只以主纜鋼量最省選擇大垂度，塔高與塔底彎矩可能增加到基礎難以承受，也延長塔施工與高空作業時間；反之垂度過小，主纜張力與錨碇規模暴增，錨碇基礎可能成為控制造價的瓶頸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Choosing a large sag only to minimise cable steel can raise tower height and base moment beyond what the foundations can comfortably take and lengthen high-level tower work; too little sag inflates cable tension and anchorage size, making anchorage foundations the cost bottleneck. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b004-v13-05","title":"寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “45 m wide steel deck” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"主跨超過 2 km 時，扭轉頻率更低，單一流線形箱梁難以單靠形狀把顫振風速推得夠高。本橋橋面寬約 45 m、最大梁深約 3.5 m，提供雙向六車道與兩側維修走道，鋼箱以約 24 m 間距的橫梁連接，形成中央開口的雙箱斷面。中央開口讓上下表面的壓力在開口處部分平衡，降低驅動扭轉的氣動力矩，是近年超長跨懸索橋常用的顫振對策；代價是橫梁與開口邊緣更容易引發渦流振動，需要導流板或其他細部處理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Beyond 2 km the torsional frequency falls further and a single streamlined box can hardly push the flutter speed high enough by shape alone. This deck is about 45 m wide and up to about 3.5 m deep, carrying six traffic lanes and maintenance walkways, with steel boxes linked by cross-beams at about 24 m spacing to form a twin-box section with a central opening. The opening partly equalises pressure between upper and lower surfaces, reducing the aerodynamic moment that drives torsion, a common flutter measure on recent super-long suspension spans; the price is that cross-beams and opening edges are more prone to vortex-induced vibration, needing guide vanes or other detailing. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “45 m wide steel deck” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：顫振臨界折減風速 V_r = U_F/(f_T·B)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Critical reduced flutter velocity V_r = U_F/(f_T·B).","failure":"常見誤解：「橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “45 m wide steel deck”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-05-k1","title":"寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略","titleEn":"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck","text":"主跨超過 2 km 時，扭轉頻率更低，單一流線形箱梁難以單靠形狀把顫振風速推得夠高。本橋橋面寬約 45 m、最大梁深約 3.5 m，提供雙向六車道與兩側維修走道，鋼箱以約 24 m 間距的橫梁連接，形成中央開口的雙箱斷面。","textEn":"Beyond 2 km the torsional frequency falls further and a single streamlined box can hardly push the flutter speed high enough by shape alone. This deck is about 45 m wide and up to about 3.5 m deep, carrying six traffic lanes and maintenance walkways, with steel boxes linked by cross-beams at about 24 m spacing to form a twin-box section with a central opening.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck\" is correct?","options":["橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。","只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。","主跨超過 2 km 時，扭轉頻率更低，單一流線形箱梁難以單靠形狀把顫振風速推得夠高。"],"optionsEn":["An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance.","As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.","Beyond 2 km the torsional frequency falls further and a single streamlined box can hardly push the flutter speed high enough by shape alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"主跨超過 2 km 時，扭轉頻率更低，單一流線形箱梁難以單靠形狀把顫振風速推得夠高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Beyond 2 km the torsional frequency falls further and a single streamlined box can hardly push the flutter speed high enough by shape alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b004-v13-06","title":"寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “45 m wide steel deck” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：顫振臨界折減風速 V_r = U_F/(f_T·B)。取 f_T = 0.12 Hz、B = 45 m：若斷面 V_r = 13，U_F = 13×0.12×45 ≈ 70 m/s；中央開口若把 V_r 提高到 15，U_F ≈ 81 m/s，提升約 15%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Critical reduced flutter velocity V_r = U_F/(f_T·B). With f_T = 0.12 Hz and B = 45 m: a section with V_r = 13 gives U_F = 13×0.12×45 ≈ 70 m/s; if the central opening raises V_r to 15, U_F ≈ 81 m/s, about 15% higher. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較封閉單箱與不同開口寬度的斷面模型，量測氣動導數與渦振鎖定風速範圍；選定斷面後檢查各風攻角的顫振臨界風速與渦振振幅，並以使用性準則（例如行車舒適的加速度限值）評估渦振。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare section models of a closed single box and several opening widths, measuring aerodynamic derivatives and vortex lock-in ranges; for the chosen section check flutter onset at each angle of attack and vortex amplitudes against serviceability criteria such as driver-comfort acceleration limits.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"顫振臨界折減風速 V_r = U_F/(f_T·B)。取 f_T = 0.12 Hz、B = 45 m：若斷面 V_r = 13，U_F = 13×0.12×45 ≈ 70 m/s；中央開口若把 V_r 提高到 15，U_F ≈ 81 m/s，提升約 15%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Critical reduced flutter velocity V_r = U_F/(f_T·B). With f_T = 0.12 Hz and B = 45 m: a section with V_r = 13 gives U_F = 13×0.12×45 ≈ 70 m/s; if the central opening raises V_r to 15, U_F ≈ 81 m/s, about 15% higher. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck\", which statement holds?","options":["顫振臨界折減風速 V_r = U_F/(f_T·B)。","沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。","模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Critical reduced flutter velocity V_r = U_F/(f_T·B).","A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check.","If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顫振臨界折減風速 V_r = U_F/(f_T·B)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Critical reduced flutter velocity V_r = U_F/(f_T·B). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b004-v13-07","title":"寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “45 m wide steel deck” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較封閉單箱與不同開口寬度的斷面模型，量測氣動導數與渦振鎖定風速範圍；選定斷面後檢查各風攻角的顫振臨界風速與渦振振幅，並以使用性準則（例如行車舒適的加速度限值）評估渦振。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare section models of a closed single box and several opening widths, measuring aerodynamic derivatives and vortex lock-in ranges; for the chosen section check flutter onset at each angle of attack and vortex amplitudes against serviceability criteria such as driver-comfort acceleration limits. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：欄杆、隔音牆、維修車軌道等附屬物的形狀與透空率必須在風洞試驗前凍結；施工期間任何附屬物變更都須回送風工程師確認，並在竣工圖中標明經試驗的斷面版本。","observationEn":"Site practice: Freeze the shape and porosity of railings, screens and gantry rails before wind-tunnel testing; any change during construction goes back to the wind engineer, and the as-built drawings must identify the tested section version.","failure":"注意干擾：開口斷面若未處理橫梁與欄杆細部，中低風速時可能出現持續的豎向渦振，雖不危及強度卻造成用路人不適與疲勞循環；大貝爾特東橋通車後即因箱梁渦振加裝導流板。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If cross-beams and railings on a twin-box section are not detailed, persistent vertical vortex vibration can appear at moderate wind speeds, harmless to strength but uncomfortable for drivers and a source of fatigue cycles; the Great Belt East Bridge had guide vanes added after opening for box-girder vortex vibration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較封閉單箱與不同開口寬度的斷面模型，量測氣動導數與渦振鎖定風速範圍；選定斷面後檢查各風攻角的顫振臨界風速與渦振振幅，並以使用性準則（例如行車舒適的加速度限值）評估渦振。","textEn":"Compare section models of a closed single box and several opening widths, measuring aerodynamic derivatives and vortex lock-in ranges; for the chosen section check flutter onset at each angle of attack and vortex amplitudes against serviceability criteria such as driver-comfort acceleration limits.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"欄杆、隔音牆、維修車軌道等附屬物的形狀與透空率必須在風洞試驗前凍結；施工期間任何附屬物變更都須回送風工程師確認，並在竣工圖中標明經試驗的斷面版本。","textEn":"Freeze the shape and porosity of railings, screens and gantry rails before wind-tunnel testing; any change during construction goes back to the wind engineer, and the as-built drawings must identify the tested section version.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較封閉單箱與不同開口寬度的斷面模型，量測氣動導數與渦振鎖定風速範圍。","主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Compare section models of a closed single box and several opening widths, measuring aerodynamic derivatives and vortex lock-in ranges.","The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較封閉單箱與不同開口寬度的斷面模型，量測氣動導數與渦振鎖定風速範圍；選定斷面後檢查各風攻角的顫振臨界風速與渦振振幅，並以使用性準則（例如行車舒適的加速度限值）評估渦振。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare section models of a closed single box and several opening widths, measuring aerodynamic derivatives and vortex lock-in ranges; for the chosen section check flutter onset at each angle of attack and vortex amplitudes against serviceability criteria such as driver-comfort acceleration limits. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b004-v13-08","title":"寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「45 m 寬鋼箱梁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “45 m wide steel deck” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"開口斷面若未處理橫梁與欄杆細部，中低風速時可能出現持續的豎向渦振，雖不危及強度卻造成用路人不適與疲勞循環；大貝爾特東橋通車後即因箱梁渦振加裝導流板。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If cross-beams and railings on a twin-box section are not detailed, persistent vertical vortex vibration can appear at moderate wind speeds, harmless to strength but uncomfortable for drivers and a source of fatigue cycles; the Great Belt East Bridge had guide vanes added after opening for box-girder vortex vibration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：中央開口讓上下表面的壓力在開口處部分平衡，降低驅動扭轉的氣動力矩，是近年超長跨懸索橋常用的顫振對策；代價是橫梁與開口邊緣更容易引發渦流振動，需要導流板或其他細部處理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The opening partly equalises pressure between upper and lower surfaces, reducing the aerodynamic moment that drives torsion, a common flutter measure on recent super-long suspension spans; the price is that cross-beams and opening edges are more prone to vortex-induced vibration, needing guide vanes or other detailing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"開口斷面若未處理橫梁與欄杆細部，中低風速時可能出現持續的豎向渦振，雖不危及強度卻造成用路人不適與疲勞循環；大貝爾特東橋通車後即因箱梁渦振加裝導流板。","textEn":"If cross-beams and railings on a twin-box section are not detailed, persistent vertical vortex vibration can appear at moderate wind speeds, harmless to strength but uncomfortable for drivers and a source of fatigue cycles; the Great Belt East Bridge had guide vanes added after opening for box-girder vortex vibration.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「寬幅雙箱梁的抗風策略」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind strategy for a wide twin-box deck\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。","開口斷面若未處理橫梁與欄杆細部，中低風速時可能出現持續的豎向渦振，雖不危及強度卻造成用路人不適與疲勞循環；大貝爾特東橋通車後即因箱梁渦振加裝導流板。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.","If cross-beams and railings on a twin-box section are not detailed, persistent vertical vortex vibration can appear at moderate wind speeds, harmless to strength but uncomfortable for drivers and a source of fatigue cycles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開口斷面若未處理橫梁與欄杆細部，中低風速時可能出現持續的豎向渦振，雖不危及強度卻造成用路人不適與疲勞循環；大貝爾特東橋通車後即因箱梁渦振加裝導流板。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If cross-beams and railings on a twin-box section are not detailed, persistent vertical vortex vibration can appear at moderate wind speeds, harmless to strength but uncomfortable for drivers and a source of fatigue cycles; the Great Belt East Bridge had guide vanes added after opening for box-girder vortex vibration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b004-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面」與「地震帶上的重力式沉箱」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire\" and \"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b004-v13-09","title":"1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “1,960 MPa parallel wire” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主刊物列出主纜鋼絲抗拉強度為 1,960 MPa 級，資料庫記載每條主纜在主跨由 144 股、每股 127 根 5.75 mm 鋼絲組成（邊跨增至 148 股以承受較大張力）。相較明石海峽大橋的約 1,770 MPa 級鋼絲，強度提高約 11%，同一張力所需鋼絲面積與自重都下降，而自重下降又回饋減少張力，這是主跨能超過 2 km 的關鍵之一。代價是鋼絲對缺口、氫脆與疲勞更敏感，對鍍層、製造品管與防蝕的要求同步提高。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The owner's publication gives the cable wire strength as the 1,960 MPa class, and a structures database records each main cable in the main span as 144 strands of 127 wires of 5.75 mm (rising to 148 strands in the side spans to carry their higher tension). Compared with the roughly 1,770 MPa class wire of Akashi Kaikyo this is about 11% stronger, so the wire area and self-weight for a given tension fall, and the lower self-weight feeds back into lower tension, one of the keys to exceeding 2 km. The price is greater sensitivity to notches, hydrogen embrittlement and fatigue, raising demands on coating, manufacturing control and corrosion protection. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “1,960 MPa parallel wire” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單絲面積 π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm²，144×127 = 18,288 根，A ≈ 474,900 mm²，破斷力 ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Wire area π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm², with 144×127 = 18,288 wires, A ≈ 474,900 mm² and breaking force ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “1,960 MPa parallel wire”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-09-k1","title":"1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面","titleEn":"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire","text":"業主刊物列出主纜鋼絲抗拉強度為 1,960 MPa 級，資料庫記載每條主纜在主跨由 144 股、每股 127 根 5.75 mm 鋼絲組成（邊跨增至 148 股以承受較大張力）。相較明石海峽大橋的約 1,770 MPa 級鋼絲，強度提高約 11%，同一張力所需鋼絲面積與自重都下降，而自重下降又回饋減少張力，這是主跨能超過 2 km 的關鍵之一。","textEn":"The owner's publication gives the cable wire strength as the 1,960 MPa class, and a structures database records each main cable in the main span as 144 strands of 127 wires of 5.75 mm (rising to 148 strands in the side spans to carry their higher tension). Compared with the roughly 1,770 MPa class wire of Akashi Kaikyo this is about 11% stronger, so the wire area and self-weight for a given tension fall, and the lower self-weight feeds back into lower tension, one of the keys to exceeding 2 km.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire\" is correct?","options":["業主刊物列出主纜鋼絲抗拉強度為 1,960 MPa 級，資料庫記載每條主纜在主跨由 144 股、每股 127 根 5.75 mm 鋼絲組成（邊跨增至 148 股以承受較大張力）。","只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。","基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。"],"optionsEn":["The owner's publication gives the cable wire strength as the 1,960 MPa class, and a structures database records each main cable in the main span as 144 strands of 127 wires of 5.75 mm (rising to 148 strands in the side spans to carry their higher tension).","As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.","If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"業主刊物列出主纜鋼絲抗拉強度為 1,960 MPa 級，資料庫記載每條主纜在主跨由 144 股、每股 127 根 5.75 mm 鋼絲組成（邊跨增至 148 股以承受較大張力）。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The owner's publication gives the cable wire strength as the 1,960 MPa class, and a structures database records each main cable in the main span as 144 strands of 127 wires of 5.75 mm (rising to 148 strands in the side spans to carry their higher tension). The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b004-v13-10","title":"1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “1,960 MPa parallel wire” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單絲面積 π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm²，144×127 = 18,288 根，A ≈ 474,900 mm²，破斷力 ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN。若空隙率 20%，主纜外徑 ≈ √(4×0.594/π) ≈ 0.87 m；鋼絲自重 0.4749×7,850 ≈ 3.73 t/m。改用 1,770 MPa 鋼絲提供同破斷力需面積多約 10.7%。空隙率為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Wire area π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm², with 144×127 = 18,288 wires, A ≈ 474,900 mm² and breaking force ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN. With a 20% void ratio the cable diameter is ≈ √(4×0.594/π) ≈ 0.87 m; wire self-weight is 0.4749×7,850 ≈ 3.73 t/m. Supplying the same force with 1,770 MPa wire needs about 10.7% more area. The void ratio is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鋼絲規格須涵蓋抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與彎曲試驗、鍍層附著量與均勻性；每股完成後檢查長度標記與錨頭灌注，抽樣做錨頭拉拔與疲勞試驗；架設後以纜徑與周長量測核算空隙率是否在設計範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The wire specification must cover tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and bend tests, coating mass and uniformity; check length marks and socket filling on every strand, sample sockets for pull-out and fatigue tests, and after erection compute void ratio from measured diameter and circumference against the design range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單絲面積 π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm²，144×127 = 18,288 根，A ≈ 474,900 mm²，破斷力 ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN。若空隙率 20%，主纜外徑 ≈ √(4×0.594/π) ≈ 0.87 m；鋼絲自重 0.4749×7,850 ≈ 3.73 t/m。改用 1,770 MPa 鋼絲提供同破斷力需面積多約 10.7%。空隙率為教學假設。","textEn":"Wire area π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm², with 144×127 = 18,288 wires, A ≈ 474,900 mm² and breaking force ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN. With a 20% void ratio the cable diameter is ≈ √(4×0.594/π) ≈ 0.87 m; wire self-weight is 0.4749×7,850 ≈ 3.73 t/m. Supplying the same force with 1,770 MPa wire needs about 10.7% more area. The void ratio is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire\", which statement holds?","options":["索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","單絲面積 π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm²，144×127 = 18,288 根，A ≈ 474,900 mm²，破斷力 ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN。","只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。"],"optionsEn":["Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","Wire area π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm², with 144×127 = 18,288 wires, A ≈ 474,900 mm² and breaking force ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN.","One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單絲面積 π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm²，144×127 = 18,288 根，A ≈ 474,900 mm²，破斷力 ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Wire area π/4×5.75² = 25.97 mm², with 144×127 = 18,288 wires, A ≈ 474,900 mm² and breaking force ≈ 474,900×1,960 ≈ 931 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b004-v13-11","title":"1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “1,960 MPa parallel wire” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鋼絲規格須涵蓋抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與彎曲試驗、鍍層附著量與均勻性；每股完成後檢查長度標記與錨頭灌注，抽樣做錨頭拉拔與疲勞試驗；架設後以纜徑與周長量測核算空隙率是否在設計範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The wire specification must cover tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and bend tests, coating mass and uniformity; check length marks and socket filling on every strand, sample sockets for pull-out and fatigue tests, and after erection compute void ratio from measured diameter and circumference against the design range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對 1,960 MPa 級鋼絲，採購應要求製程資格試驗、批次追溯與第三方見證，並把延性、扭轉與鍍層試驗的不合格處理流程寫清楚；運輸與牽引機具接觸面須加保護墊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For 1,960 MPa class wire, procurement should require process qualification tests, batch traceability and third-party witnessing, with a written procedure for ductility, torsion or coating test failures; protect every contact surface of transport and hauling equipment with pads.","failure":"注意干擾：超高強度鋼絲若伸長率或扭轉性能不足，會在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處提早斷絲；鍍層不均或運輸刮傷則讓腐蝕坑成為疲勞與氫脆的起點，斷絲往往在多年後才在內部檢查中發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ultra-high-strength wire with inadequate elongation or torsion performance can break early where it bends locally at saddles or cable bands; uneven coating or transport scratches make corrosion pits the starting point for fatigue and hydrogen embrittlement, and broken wires are often found only years later during internal inspection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鋼絲規格須涵蓋抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與彎曲試驗、鍍層附著量與均勻性；每股完成後檢查長度標記與錨頭灌注，抽樣做錨頭拉拔與疲勞試驗；架設後以纜徑與周長量測核算空隙率是否在設計範圍。","textEn":"The wire specification must cover tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and bend tests, coating mass and uniformity; check length marks and socket filling on every strand, sample sockets for pull-out and fatigue tests, and after erection compute void ratio from measured diameter and circumference against the design range.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對 1,960 MPa 級鋼絲，採購應要求製程資格試驗、批次追溯與第三方見證，並把延性、扭轉與鍍層試驗的不合格處理流程寫清楚；運輸與牽引機具接觸面須加保護墊。","textEn":"For 1,960 MPa class wire, procurement should require process qualification tests, batch traceability and third-party witnessing, with a written procedure for ductility, torsion or coating test failures; protect every contact surface of transport and hauling equipment with pads.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。","鋼絲規格須涵蓋抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與彎曲試驗、鍍層附著量與均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter.","The wire specification must cover tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and bend tests, coating mass and uniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼絲規格須涵蓋抗拉強度、0.2% 耐力、伸長率、扭轉與彎曲試驗、鍍層附著量與均勻性；每股完成後檢查長度標記與錨頭灌注，抽樣做錨頭拉拔與疲勞試驗；架設後以纜徑與周長量測核算空隙率是否在設計範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The wire specification must cover tensile strength, 0.2% proof stress, elongation, torsion and bend tests, coating mass and uniformity; check length marks and socket filling on every strand, sample sockets for pull-out and fatigue tests, and after erection compute void ratio from measured diameter and circumference against the design range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b004-v13-12","title":"1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「1,960 MPa 平行鋼絲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “1,960 MPa parallel wire” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"超高強度鋼絲若伸長率或扭轉性能不足，會在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處提早斷絲；鍍層不均或運輸刮傷則讓腐蝕坑成為疲勞與氫脆的起點，斷絲往往在多年後才在內部檢查中發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ultra-high-strength wire with inadequate elongation or torsion performance can break early where it bends locally at saddles or cable bands; uneven coating or transport scratches make corrosion pits the starting point for fatigue and hydrogen embrittlement, and broken wires are often found only years later during internal inspection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：代價是鋼絲對缺口、氫脆與疲勞更敏感，對鍍層、製造品管與防蝕的要求同步提高。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The price is greater sensitivity to notches, hydrogen embrittlement and fatigue, raising demands on coating, manufacturing control and corrosion protection.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"超高強度鋼絲若伸長率或扭轉性能不足，會在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處提早斷絲；鍍層不均或運輸刮傷則讓腐蝕坑成為疲勞與氫脆的起點，斷絲往往在多年後才在內部檢查中發現。","textEn":"Ultra-high-strength wire with inadequate elongation or torsion performance can break early where it bends locally at saddles or cable bands; uneven coating or transport scratches make corrosion pits the starting point for fatigue and hydrogen embrittlement, and broken wires are often found only years later during internal inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「1,960 MPa 鋼絲的主纜斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Main-cable section with 1,960 MPa wire\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["超高強度鋼絲若伸長率或扭轉性能不足，會在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處提早斷絲。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。"],"optionsEn":["Ultra-high-strength wire with inadequate elongation or torsion performance can break early where it bends locally at saddles or cable bands.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"超高強度鋼絲若伸長率或扭轉性能不足，會在索鞍或索夾附近的局部彎曲處提早斷絲；鍍層不均或運輸刮傷則讓腐蝕坑成為疲勞與氫脆的起點，斷絲往往在多年後才在內部檢查中發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ultra-high-strength wire with inadequate elongation or torsion performance can break early where it bends locally at saddles or cable bands; uneven coating or transport scratches make corrosion pits the starting point for fatigue and hydrogen embrittlement, and broken wires are often found only years later during internal inspection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b004-v13-13","title":"地震帶上的重力式沉箱：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「隔震式沉箱基礎」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Isolated caisson foundation” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"達達尼爾海峽位於北安那托利亞斷層系統附近的地震活躍區，主塔基礎必須在不可預期的地震中保護 318 m 鋼塔。業主刊物指出本橋採用「隔震式基礎」以提高耐震性；這類重力式沉箱放在整平的碎石墊層上而不以樁與岩盤固接，地震時若水平力超過墊層摩擦抗力，沉箱允許少量滑動，等於為傳入塔身的水平力設定上限。設計要同時檢核承載、沉陷、滑動位移與滑動後的殘餘傾斜。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隔震式沉箱基礎」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Dardanelles lie in an active seismic region near the North Anatolian Fault system, and the tower foundations must protect 318 m steel towers in unpredictable earthquakes. The owner's publication states that an isolated foundation was used to improve seismic resistance; such gravity caissons rest on a levelled gravel bed rather than being fixed to rock by piles, so if the horizontal force exceeds the bed's friction resistance in an earthquake the caisson may slide slightly, capping the horizontal force passed into the tower. Design must check bearing, settlement, sliding displacement and residual tilt after sliding together. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Isolated caisson foundation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：滑動上限 H_max = μ·N'。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Sliding cap H_max = μ·N'.","failure":"常見誤解：「基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隔震式沉箱基礎」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Isolated caisson foundation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-13-k1","title":"地震帶上的重力式沉箱","titleEn":"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone","text":"達達尼爾海峽位於北安那托利亞斷層系統附近的地震活躍區，主塔基礎必須在不可預期的地震中保護 318 m 鋼塔。業主刊物指出本橋採用「隔震式基礎」以提高耐震性；這類重力式沉箱放在整平的碎石墊層上而不以樁與岩盤固接，地震時若水平力超過墊層摩擦抗力，沉箱允許少量滑動，等於為傳入塔身的水平力設定上限。","textEn":"The Dardanelles lie in an active seismic region near the North Anatolian Fault system, and the tower foundations must protect 318 m steel towers in unpredictable earthquakes. The owner's publication states that an isolated foundation was used to improve seismic resistance; such gravity caissons rest on a levelled gravel bed rather than being fixed to rock by piles, so if the horizontal force exceeds the bed's friction resistance in an earthquake the caisson may slide slightly, capping the horizontal force passed into the tower.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震帶上的重力式沉箱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone\" is correct?","options":["基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。","達達尼爾海峽位於北安那托利亞斷層系統附近的地震活躍區，主塔基礎必須在不可預期的地震中保護 318 m 鋼塔。","沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。"],"optionsEn":["If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed.","The Dardanelles lie in an active seismic region near the North Anatolian Fault system, and the tower foundations must protect 318 m steel towers in unpredictable earthquakes.","A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"達達尼爾海峽位於北安那托利亞斷層系統附近的地震活躍區，主塔基礎必須在不可預期的地震中保護 318 m 鋼塔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Dardanelles lie in an active seismic region near the North Anatolian Fault system, and the tower foundations must protect 318 m steel towers in unpredictable earthquakes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b004-v13-14","title":"地震帶上的重力式沉箱：定量估算","titleEn":"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔震式沉箱基礎」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Isolated caisson foundation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：滑動上限 H_max = μ·N'。取有效垂直力 N' = 2,000 MN、碎石墊層摩擦係數 μ = 0.6，H_max = 1,200 MN。若沉箱含附加水質量 M = 280,000 t、地表加速度 0.5 g，剛性需求 M·a = 280×10⁶×4.905 ≈ 1,373 MN > 1,200 MN，沉箱會滑動，傳入上部的力被限制在約 1,200 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Sliding cap H_max = μ·N'. With effective vertical force N' = 2,000 MN and gravel-bed friction μ = 0.6, H_max = 1,200 MN. For a caisson with added-water mass M = 280,000 t and 0.5 g ground acceleration the rigid demand M·a = 280×10⁶×4.905 ≈ 1,373 MN > 1,200 MN, so the caisson slides and the force passed upward is limited to about 1,200 MN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層與遠域地震紀錄，求滑動位移、轉角與塔頂殘餘位移，與容許值比較；碎石墊層的摩擦係數以大型直剪或現地試驗確認，鋪設後以多音束測深檢查平整度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several near-fault and far-field records to obtain sliding displacement, rotation and residual tower-top offset against allowable values; confirm gravel-bed friction by large direct-shear or field tests, and check bed flatness by multibeam survey after placement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"滑動上限 H_max = μ·N'。取有效垂直力 N' = 2,000 MN、碎石墊層摩擦係數 μ = 0.6，H_max = 1,200 MN。若沉箱含附加水質量 M = 280,000 t、地表加速度 0.5 g，剛性需求 M·a = 280×10⁶×4.905 ≈ 1,373 MN > 1,200 MN，沉箱會滑動，傳入上部的力被限制在約 1,200 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Sliding cap H_max = μ·N'. With effective vertical force N' = 2,000 MN and gravel-bed friction μ = 0.6, H_max = 1,200 MN. For a caisson with added-water mass M = 280,000 t and 0.5 g ground acceleration the rigid demand M·a = 280×10⁶×4.905 ≈ 1,373 MN > 1,200 MN, so the caisson slides and the force passed upward is limited to about 1,200 MN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震帶上的重力式沉箱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone\", which statement holds?","options":["模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。","主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。","滑動上限 H_max = μ·N'。"],"optionsEn":["If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter.","The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.","Sliding cap H_max = μ·N'."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑動上限 H_max = μ·N'。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Sliding cap H_max = μ·N'. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b004-v13-15","title":"地震帶上的重力式沉箱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔震式沉箱基礎」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Isolated caisson foundation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層與遠域地震紀錄，求滑動位移、轉角與塔頂殘餘位移，與容許值比較；碎石墊層的摩擦係數以大型直剪或現地試驗確認，鋪設後以多音束測深檢查平整度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several near-fault and far-field records to obtain sliding displacement, rotation and residual tower-top offset against allowable values; confirm gravel-bed friction by large direct-shear or field tests, and check bed flatness by multibeam survey after placement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：墊層材料、級配、鋪設厚度與平整度允差應作為沉箱沉放前的停留點，由設計者與第三方驗證單位共同簽認；營運期應保存基礎座標與傾斜基準，以便地震後快速比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Gravel material, grading, thickness and flatness tolerance should be a hold point before caisson placement, signed jointly by the designer and the independent checker; in service keep foundation coordinate and tilt baselines for rapid post-earthquake comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：若墊層摩擦係數被高估，實際滑動門檻偏高，塔身承受比設計更大的地震力；若墊層不平或局部軟弱，沉箱沉放後可能產生初始傾斜，地震滑動時再放大殘餘傾斜，影響主纜幾何與伸縮縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overestimating bed friction raises the real sliding threshold so the tower sees larger seismic forces than designed; an uneven or locally soft bed can give the caisson an initial tilt after placement that grows during seismic sliding, disturbing cable geometry and expansion joints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層與遠域地震紀錄，求滑動位移、轉角與塔頂殘餘位移，與容許值比較；碎石墊層的摩擦係數以大型直剪或現地試驗確認，鋪設後以多音束測深檢查平整度。","textEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several near-fault and far-field records to obtain sliding displacement, rotation and residual tower-top offset against allowable values; confirm gravel-bed friction by large direct-shear or field tests, and check bed flatness by multibeam survey after placement.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"墊層材料、級配、鋪設厚度與平整度允差應作為沉箱沉放前的停留點，由設計者與第三方驗證單位共同簽認；營運期應保存基礎座標與傾斜基準，以便地震後快速比對。","textEn":"Gravel material, grading, thickness and flatness tolerance should be a hold point before caisson placement, signed jointly by the designer and the independent checker; in service keep foundation coordinate and tilt baselines for rapid post-earthquake comparison.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震帶上的重力式沉箱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone\"?","options":["以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層與遠域地震紀錄，求滑動位移、轉角與塔頂殘餘位移，與容許值比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。"],"optionsEn":["Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several near-fault and far-field records to obtain sliding displacement, rotation and residual tower-top offset against allowable values.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入多組近斷層與遠域地震紀錄，求滑動位移、轉角與塔頂殘餘位移，與容許值比較；碎石墊層的摩擦係數以大型直剪或現地試驗確認，鋪設後以多音束測深檢查平整度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with several near-fault and far-field records to obtain sliding displacement, rotation and residual tower-top offset against allowable values; confirm gravel-bed friction by large direct-shear or field tests, and check bed flatness by multibeam survey after placement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b004-v13-16","title":"地震帶上的重力式沉箱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔震式沉箱基礎」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Isolated caisson foundation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若墊層摩擦係數被高估，實際滑動門檻偏高，塔身承受比設計更大的地震力；若墊層不平或局部軟弱，沉箱沉放後可能產生初始傾斜，地震滑動時再放大殘餘傾斜，影響主纜幾何與伸縮縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overestimating bed friction raises the real sliding threshold so the tower sees larger seismic forces than designed; an uneven or locally soft bed can give the caisson an initial tilt after placement that grows during seismic sliding, disturbing cable geometry and expansion joints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計要同時檢核承載、沉陷、滑動位移與滑動後的殘餘傾斜。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Design must check bearing, settlement, sliding displacement and residual tilt after sliding together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若墊層摩擦係數被高估，實際滑動門檻偏高，塔身承受比設計更大的地震力；若墊層不平或局部軟弱，沉箱沉放後可能產生初始傾斜，地震滑動時再放大殘餘傾斜，影響主纜幾何與伸縮縫。","textEn":"Overestimating bed friction raises the real sliding threshold so the tower sees larger seismic forces than designed; an uneven or locally soft bed can give the caisson an initial tilt after placement that grows during seismic sliding, disturbing cable geometry and expansion joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震帶上的重力式沉箱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gravity caissons in a seismic zone\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若墊層摩擦係數被高估，實際滑動門檻偏高，塔身承受比設計更大的地震力。","沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Overestimating bed friction raises the real sliding threshold so the tower sees larger seismic forces than designed.","A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若墊層摩擦係數被高估，實際滑動門檻偏高，塔身承受比設計更大的地震力；若墊層不平或局部軟弱，沉箱沉放後可能產生初始傾斜，地震滑動時再放大殘餘傾斜，影響主纜幾何與伸縮縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overestimating bed friction raises the real sliding threshold so the tower sees larger seismic forces than designed; an uneven or locally soft bed can give the caisson an initial tilt after placement that grows during seismic sliding, disturbing cable geometry and expansion joints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b004-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放」與「橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Caisson casting, towing and immersion\" and \"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b004-v13-17","title":"沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Caisson casting, towing and immersion: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「乾塢預製與拖航」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dry-dock casting and tow” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主時間軸記載 2019 年 1 月沉箱由乾塢拖往濕塢，同年 4 月與 5 月分別完成歐洲側與亞洲側沉箱上的鋼塔基段安裝。這種流程讓大部分混凝土在乾塢或靠岸位置完成，再以拖船把漂浮沉箱拖到塔位、逐艙灌水沉放到預先整平的墊層上。漂浮期間沉箱必須有足夠穩性抵抗風浪傾覆，沉放時則要控制各艙水位使沉箱水平下降，最後就位誤差通常以公分計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「乾塢預製與拖航」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The owner's timeline records the caissons being towed from the dry dock to the wet dock in January 2019, with the steel shaft installation on the European and Asian caissons completed in April and May of that year. This sequence completes most concrete in the dry dock or alongside a quay, after which tugs tow the floating caisson to the tower site and it is ballasted compartment by compartment onto the levelled bed. Afloat, the caisson needs enough stability to resist capsizing in wind and waves; during immersion compartment water levels are controlled so it descends level, and final positioning error is usually measured in centimetres. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dry-dock casting and tow” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A_p)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A_p).","failure":"常見誤解：「沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「乾塢預製與拖航」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dry-dock casting and tow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-17-k1","title":"沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放","titleEn":"Caisson casting, towing and immersion","text":"業主時間軸記載 2019 年 1 月沉箱由乾塢拖往濕塢，同年 4 月與 5 月分別完成歐洲側與亞洲側沉箱上的鋼塔基段安裝。這種流程讓大部分混凝土在乾塢或靠岸位置完成，再以拖船把漂浮沉箱拖到塔位、逐艙灌水沉放到預先整平的墊層上。","textEn":"The owner's timeline records the caissons being towed from the dry dock to the wet dock in January 2019, with the steel shaft installation on the European and Asian caissons completed in April and May of that year. This sequence completes most concrete in the dry dock or alongside a quay, after which tugs tow the floating caisson to the tower site and it is ballasted compartment by compartment onto the levelled bed.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Caisson casting, towing and immersion\" is correct?","options":["沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。","索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","業主時間軸記載 2019 年 1 月沉箱由乾塢拖往濕塢，同年 4 月與 5 月分別完成歐洲側與亞洲側沉箱上的鋼塔基段安裝。"],"optionsEn":["A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check.","Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","The owner's timeline records the caissons being towed from the dry dock to the wet dock in January 2019, with the steel shaft installation on the European and Asian caissons completed in April and May of that year."],"answer":2,"explanation":"業主時間軸記載 2019 年 1 月沉箱由乾塢拖往濕塢，同年 4 月與 5 月分別完成歐洲側與亞洲側沉箱上的鋼塔基段安裝。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The owner's timeline records the caissons being towed from the dry dock to the wet dock in January 2019, with the steel shaft installation on the European and Asian caissons completed in April and May of that year. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b004-v13-18","title":"沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放：定量估算","titleEn":"Caisson casting, towing and immersion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「乾塢預製與拖航」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dry-dock casting and tow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A_p)。設平面 70 m × 80 m、拖航重量 75,000 t：V = 75,000/1.025 ≈ 73,170 m³，d ≈ 13.1 m。穩心高 GM = KB + BM − KG，BM = I/V = (70³×80/12)/73,170 ≈ 31.3 m，KB ≈ 6.5 m，KG 取 15 m，GM ≈ 22.8 m > 0，穩定。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A_p). For a 70 m × 80 m plan and a 75,000 t towing weight: V = 75,000/1.025 ≈ 73,170 m³ and d ≈ 13.1 m. Metacentric height GM = KB + BM − KG, with BM = I/V = (70³×80/12)/73,170 ≈ 31.3 m, KB ≈ 6.5 m and KG taken as 15 m, gives GM ≈ 22.8 m > 0, stable. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：拖航前由海事檢驗單位核可穩性計算、拖航路線與氣象窗口；沉放過程以 GNSS、傾斜儀與各艙水位計即時監控，就位後以水下測量確認平面位置、高程與傾斜，與允差比較後才可灌注壓艙材料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before towing, a marine warranty surveyor approves stability calculations, tow route and weather window; during immersion monitor GNSS, inclinometers and compartment levels in real time, and after landing confirm position, level and tilt by underwater survey against tolerances before permanent ballast is placed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A_p)。設平面 70 m × 80 m、拖航重量 75,000 t：V = 75,000/1.025 ≈ 73,170 m³，d ≈ 13.1 m。穩心高 GM = KB + BM − KG，BM = I/V = (70³×80/12)/73,170 ≈ 31.3 m，KB ≈ 6.5 m，KG 取 15 m，GM ≈ 22.8 m > 0，穩定。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A_p). For a 70 m × 80 m plan and a 75,000 t towing weight: V = 75,000/1.025 ≈ 73,170 m³ and d ≈ 13.1 m. Metacentric height GM = KB + BM − KG, with BM = I/V = (70³×80/12)/73,170 ≈ 31.3 m, KB ≈ 6.5 m and KG taken as 15 m, gives GM ≈ 22.8 m > 0, stable. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Caisson casting, towing and immersion\", which statement holds?","options":["吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A_p)。","只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。","伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。"],"optionsEn":["Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A_p).","One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely.","An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A_p)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A_p). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b004-v13-19","title":"沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Caisson casting, towing and immersion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「乾塢預製與拖航」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dry-dock casting and tow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"拖航前由海事檢驗單位核可穩性計算、拖航路線與氣象窗口；沉放過程以 GNSS、傾斜儀與各艙水位計即時監控，就位後以水下測量確認平面位置、高程與傾斜，與允差比較後才可灌注壓艙材料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before towing, a marine warranty surveyor approves stability calculations, tow route and weather window; during immersion monitor GNSS, inclinometers and compartment levels in real time, and after landing confirm position, level and tilt by underwater survey against tolerances before permanent ballast is placed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：拖航與沉放須有書面的氣象與海況停止條件、各艙灌水順序表與緊急程序，並由海事保證檢驗人員簽發許可；每一階段的實測吃水與傾斜要與計算值比對並記錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Towing and immersion need written weather and sea-state stop criteria, a compartment ballasting table and emergency procedures, with approval issued by the marine warranty surveyor; compare and log measured draft and tilt at every stage against calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：各艙灌水不同步會讓沉箱傾斜，自由液面效應降低穩心高，嚴重時可能失穩；若在海流或風浪超過預報時強行沉放，沉箱可能偏離墊層或撞擊已鋪設的碎石，造成就位誤差與墊層損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronised ballasting tilts the caisson and free-surface effects reduce metacentric height, possibly to instability; forcing immersion when currents or waves exceed the forecast can push the caisson off the bed or scour the placed gravel, causing positioning error and bed damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"拖航前由海事檢驗單位核可穩性計算、拖航路線與氣象窗口；沉放過程以 GNSS、傾斜儀與各艙水位計即時監控，就位後以水下測量確認平面位置、高程與傾斜，與允差比較後才可灌注壓艙材料。","textEn":"Before towing, a marine warranty surveyor approves stability calculations, tow route and weather window; during immersion monitor GNSS, inclinometers and compartment levels in real time, and after landing confirm position, level and tilt by underwater survey against tolerances before permanent ballast is placed.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"拖航與沉放須有書面的氣象與海況停止條件、各艙灌水順序表與緊急程序，並由海事保證檢驗人員簽發許可；每一階段的實測吃水與傾斜要與計算值比對並記錄。","textEn":"Towing and immersion need written weather and sea-state stop criteria, a compartment ballasting table and emergency procedures, with approval issued by the marine warranty surveyor; compare and log measured draft and tilt at every stage against calculation.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Caisson casting, towing and immersion\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","拖航前由海事檢驗單位核可穩性計算、拖航路線與氣象窗口。","橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before towing, a marine warranty surveyor approves stability calculations, tow route and weather window.","An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拖航前由海事檢驗單位核可穩性計算、拖航路線與氣象窗口；沉放過程以 GNSS、傾斜儀與各艙水位計即時監控，就位後以水下測量確認平面位置、高程與傾斜，與允差比較後才可灌注壓艙材料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before towing, a marine warranty surveyor approves stability calculations, tow route and weather window; during immersion monitor GNSS, inclinometers and compartment levels in real time, and after landing confirm position, level and tilt by underwater survey against tolerances before permanent ballast is placed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b004-v13-20","title":"沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放：失效診斷","titleEn":"Caisson casting, towing and immersion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「乾塢預製與拖航」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dry-dock casting and tow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各艙灌水不同步會讓沉箱傾斜，自由液面效應降低穩心高，嚴重時可能失穩；若在海流或風浪超過預報時強行沉放，沉箱可能偏離墊層或撞擊已鋪設的碎石，造成就位誤差與墊層損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronised ballasting tilts the caisson and free-surface effects reduce metacentric height, possibly to instability; forcing immersion when currents or waves exceed the forecast can push the caisson off the bed or scour the placed gravel, causing positioning error and bed damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：漂浮期間沉箱必須有足夠穩性抵抗風浪傾覆，沉放時則要控制各艙水位使沉箱水平下降，最後就位誤差通常以公分計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Afloat, the caisson needs enough stability to resist capsizing in wind and waves; during immersion compartment water levels are controlled so it descends level, and final positioning error is usually measured in centimetres.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各艙灌水不同步會讓沉箱傾斜，自由液面效應降低穩心高，嚴重時可能失穩；若在海流或風浪超過預報時強行沉放，沉箱可能偏離墊層或撞擊已鋪設的碎石，造成就位誤差與墊層損傷。","textEn":"Unsynchronised ballasting tilts the caisson and free-surface effects reduce metacentric height, possibly to instability; forcing immersion when currents or waves exceed the forecast can push the caisson off the bed or scour the placed gravel, causing positioning error and bed damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉箱乾塢預製、拖航與沉放」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Caisson casting, towing and immersion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","各艙灌水不同步會讓沉箱傾斜，自由液面效應降低穩心高，嚴重時可能失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","Unsynchronised ballasting tilts the caisson and free-surface effects reduce metacentric height, possibly to instability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各艙灌水不同步會讓沉箱傾斜，自由液面效應降低穩心高，嚴重時可能失穩；若在海流或風浪超過預報時強行沉放，沉箱可能偏離墊層或撞擊已鋪設的碎石，造成就位誤差與墊層損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronised ballasting tilts the caisson and free-surface effects reduce metacentric height, possibly to instability; forcing immersion when currents or waves exceed the forecast can push the caisson off the bed or scour the placed gravel, causing positioning error and bed damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b004-v13-21","title":"橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Saddle preset and 87 blocks” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"業主刊物記載主跨以 87 個大小不一的橋面節塊吊起並連接到吊索，2021 年 11 月 13 日全部完成。節塊從跨中與塔邊依序吊裝時，主跨主纜荷重增加比邊跨快，若索鞍固定在塔頂，主纜不平衡水平力會把塔頂拉向主跨。因此大型懸索橋常把索鞍預先往邊跨方向偏移，隨橋面荷重增加分階段以千斤頂推回，讓塔身彎矩維持在容許範圍；節塊之間則暫時以鉸接連接，待線形接近完工狀態後再焊接封閉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The owner's publication records 87 deck blocks of various sizes lifted and connected to the hangers in the main span, all completed on 13 November 2021. As blocks are lifted from mid-span and from the towers, load on the main-span cable grows faster than on the side spans; with saddles fixed on the towers, the unbalanced horizontal force would pull the tower tops toward the main span. Large suspension bridges therefore often preset saddles toward the side spans and jack them back in stages as deck load increases, keeping tower moments within limits, while blocks are temporarily hinged together and only welded closed once the profile approaches its final state. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Saddle preset and 87 blocks” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：邊跨主纜因張力增量而伸長 ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The side-span cable stretches by ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A) as tension grows.","failure":"常見誤解：「索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Saddle preset and 87 blocks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-21-k1","title":"橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏","titleEn":"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting","text":"業主刊物記載主跨以 87 個大小不一的橋面節塊吊起並連接到吊索，2021 年 11 月 13 日全部完成。節塊從跨中與塔邊依序吊裝時，主跨主纜荷重增加比邊跨快，若索鞍固定在塔頂，主纜不平衡水平力會把塔頂拉向主跨。","textEn":"The owner's publication records 87 deck blocks of various sizes lifted and connected to the hangers in the main span, all completed on 13 November 2021. As blocks are lifted from mid-span and from the towers, load on the main-span cable grows faster than on the side spans; with saddles fixed on the towers, the unbalanced horizontal force would pull the tower tops toward the main span.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting\" is correct?","options":["業主刊物記載主跨以 87 個大小不一的橋面節塊吊起並連接到吊索，2021 年 11 月 13 日全部完成。","索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["The owner's publication records 87 deck blocks of various sizes lifted and connected to the hangers in the main span, all completed on 13 November 2021.","Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"業主刊物記載主跨以 87 個大小不一的橋面節塊吊起並連接到吊索，2021 年 11 月 13 日全部完成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The owner's publication records 87 deck blocks of various sizes lifted and connected to the hangers in the main span, all completed on 13 November 2021. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b004-v13-22","title":"橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏：定量估算","titleEn":"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Saddle preset and 87 blocks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：邊跨主纜因張力增量而伸長 ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A)。取 ΔT = 230 MN、L_s = 850 m、E = 200 GPa、A = 0.4749 m²：ΔL = 230×10⁶×850/(2×10¹¹×0.4749) ≈ 2.06 m。這是塔頂若不調整可能被拉動的量級，索鞍預偏量與分次頂推量依此規劃。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The side-span cable stretches by ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A) as tension grows. With ΔT = 230 MN, L_s = 850 m, E = 200 GPa and A = 0.4749 m²: ΔL = 230×10⁶×850/(2×10¹¹×0.4749) ≈ 2.06 m. This is the order of tower-top movement if nothing is adjusted, and saddle preset and staged jacking are planned from it. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每吊裝一批節塊後量測塔頂位移、索鞍相對位置、主纜垂度與節塊高程，與施工階段分析預測比較；塔底應力或塔頂偏位接近門檻時，依程序頂推索鞍，並記錄千斤頂力、行程與溫度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each batch of blocks, measure tower-top displacement, saddle position, cable sag and block levels against the construction-stage analysis; when tower-base stress or tower-top offset nears its trigger, jack the saddles per procedure, logging jack force, stroke and temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"邊跨主纜因張力增量而伸長 ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A)。取 ΔT = 230 MN、L_s = 850 m、E = 200 GPa、A = 0.4749 m²：ΔL = 230×10⁶×850/(2×10¹¹×0.4749) ≈ 2.06 m。這是塔頂若不調整可能被拉動的量級，索鞍預偏量與分次頂推量依此規劃。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The side-span cable stretches by ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A) as tension grows. With ΔT = 230 MN, L_s = 850 m, E = 200 GPa and A = 0.4749 m²: ΔL = 230×10⁶×850/(2×10¹¹×0.4749) ≈ 2.06 m. This is the order of tower-top movement if nothing is adjusted, and saddle preset and staged jacking are planned from it. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting\", which statement holds?","options":["主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。","邊跨主纜因張力增量而伸長 ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A)。","塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。"],"optionsEn":["The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.","The side-span cable stretches by ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A) as tension grows.","Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊跨主纜因張力增量而伸長 ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The side-span cable stretches by ΔL = ΔT·L_s/(E·A) as tension grows. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b004-v13-23","title":"橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Saddle preset and 87 blocks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每吊裝一批節塊後量測塔頂位移、索鞍相對位置、主纜垂度與節塊高程，與施工階段分析預測比較；塔底應力或塔頂偏位接近門檻時，依程序頂推索鞍，並記錄千斤頂力、行程與溫度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each batch of blocks, measure tower-top displacement, saddle position, cable sag and block levels against the construction-stage analysis; when tower-base stress or tower-top offset nears its trigger, jack the saddles per procedure, logging jack force, stroke and temperature. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工階段分析須列出每一吊裝階段的塔頂容許偏位、索鞍頂推觸發值與節塊焊接時機，形成可在現場執行的控制表；任何吊裝順序變更都要重算並由設計者核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction-stage analysis must list, for each lifting stage, the allowable tower-top offset, the saddle-jacking trigger and the block-welding window as a control table the site can follow; any change to lifting sequence must be recomputed and approved by the designer.","failure":"注意干擾：若索鞍頂推落後於吊裝進度，塔頂偏位與塔底彎矩可能超過鋼塔局部挫屈或基礎容許值；節塊過早焊接封閉，則在後續荷重下接頭承受強迫彎矩而開裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If saddle jacking lags behind lifting, tower-top offset and base moment may exceed steel-tower local buckling or foundation limits; welding blocks closed too early forces bending into the joints under later loads and can crack them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每吊裝一批節塊後量測塔頂位移、索鞍相對位置、主纜垂度與節塊高程，與施工階段分析預測比較；塔底應力或塔頂偏位接近門檻時，依程序頂推索鞍，並記錄千斤頂力、行程與溫度。","textEn":"After each batch of blocks, measure tower-top displacement, saddle position, cable sag and block levels against the construction-stage analysis; when tower-base stress or tower-top offset nears its trigger, jack the saddles per procedure, logging jack force, stroke and temperature.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工階段分析須列出每一吊裝階段的塔頂容許偏位、索鞍頂推觸發值與節塊焊接時機，形成可在現場執行的控制表；任何吊裝順序變更都要重算並由設計者核准。","textEn":"The construction-stage analysis must list, for each lifting stage, the allowable tower-top offset, the saddle-jacking trigger and the block-welding window as a control table the site can follow; any change to lifting sequence must be recomputed and approved by the designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。","每吊裝一批節塊後量測塔頂位移、索鞍相對位置、主纜垂度與節塊高程，與施工階段分析預測比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.","After each batch of blocks, measure tower-top displacement, saddle position, cable sag and block levels against the construction-stage analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每吊裝一批節塊後量測塔頂位移、索鞍相對位置、主纜垂度與節塊高程，與施工階段分析預測比較；塔底應力或塔頂偏位接近門檻時，依程序頂推索鞍，並記錄千斤頂力、行程與溫度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each batch of blocks, measure tower-top displacement, saddle position, cable sag and block levels against the construction-stage analysis; when tower-base stress or tower-top offset nears its trigger, jack the saddles per procedure, logging jack force, stroke and temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b004-v13-24","title":"橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「索鞍預偏與 87 個節塊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Saddle preset and 87 blocks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若索鞍頂推落後於吊裝進度，塔頂偏位與塔底彎矩可能超過鋼塔局部挫屈或基礎容許值；節塊過早焊接封閉，則在後續荷重下接頭承受強迫彎矩而開裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If saddle jacking lags behind lifting, tower-top offset and base moment may exceed steel-tower local buckling or foundation limits; welding blocks closed too early forces bending into the joints under later loads and can crack them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此大型懸索橋常把索鞍預先往邊跨方向偏移，隨橋面荷重增加分階段以千斤頂推回，讓塔身彎矩維持在容許範圍；節塊之間則暫時以鉸接連接，待線形接近完工狀態後再焊接封閉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large suspension bridges therefore often preset saddles toward the side spans and jack them back in stages as deck load increases, keeping tower moments within limits, while blocks are temporarily hinged together and only welded closed once the profile approaches its final state.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若索鞍頂推落後於吊裝進度，塔頂偏位與塔底彎矩可能超過鋼塔局部挫屈或基礎容許值；節塊過早焊接封閉，則在後續荷重下接頭承受強迫彎矩而開裂。","textEn":"If saddle jacking lags behind lifting, tower-top offset and base moment may exceed steel-tower local buckling or foundation limits; welding blocks closed too early forces bending into the joints under later loads and can crack them.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋面節塊吊裝與索鞍預偏」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deck-block lifting and saddle presetting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若索鞍頂推落後於吊裝進度，塔頂偏位與塔底彎矩可能超過鋼塔局部挫屈或基礎容許值；節塊過早焊接封閉，則在後續荷重下接頭承受強迫彎矩而開裂。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["If saddle jacking lags behind lifting, tower-top offset and base moment may exceed steel-tower local buckling or foundation limits.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若索鞍頂推落後於吊裝進度，塔頂偏位與塔底彎矩可能超過鋼塔局部挫屈或基礎容許值；節塊過早焊接封閉，則在後續荷重下接頭承受強迫彎矩而開裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If saddle jacking lags behind lifting, tower-top offset and base moment may exceed steel-tower local buckling or foundation limits; welding blocks closed too early forces bending into the joints under later loads and can crack them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b004-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應」與「以振動頻率驗證吊索力」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests\" and \"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b004-v13-25","title":"風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「斷面模型雷諾數」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Section-model Reynolds number” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公開資料顯示本橋的風洞試驗由加拿大邊界層風洞實驗室與丹麥 FORCE Technology 參與。斷面模型能依 Froude 或折減風速相似重現顫振與渦振，但模型雷諾數遠低於實橋，對圓角、導流板與欄杆等會影響流動分離位置的細部特別敏感。因此試驗計畫常以不同風速重複試驗觀察趨勢，必要時用加大比例的局部模型或計算流體力學輔助判讀，並以多個實驗室交叉比對結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「斷面模型雷諾數」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Public records show the bridge's wind-tunnel testing involved the Boundary Layer Wind Tunnel Laboratory in Canada and FORCE Technology in Denmark. Section models can reproduce flutter and vortex shedding through Froude or reduced-velocity similarity, but their Reynolds number is far below full scale and they are particularly sensitive to rounded corners, guide vanes and railings that set where flow separates. Test programmes therefore repeat runs at several speeds to watch trends, use larger-scale partial models or computational fluid dynamics where needed, and cross-check results between laboratories. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Section-model Reynolds number” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：雷諾數 Re = U·B/ν。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Reynolds number Re = U·B/ν.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「斷面模型雷諾數」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Section-model Reynolds number”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-25-k1","title":"風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應","titleEn":"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests","text":"公開資料顯示本橋的風洞試驗由加拿大邊界層風洞實驗室與丹麥 FORCE Technology 參與。斷面模型能依 Froude 或折減風速相似重現顫振與渦振，但模型雷諾數遠低於實橋，對圓角、導流板與欄杆等會影響流動分離位置的細部特別敏感。","textEn":"Public records show the bridge's wind-tunnel testing involved the Boundary Layer Wind Tunnel Laboratory in Canada and FORCE Technology in Denmark. Section models can reproduce flutter and vortex shedding through Froude or reduced-velocity similarity, but their Reynolds number is far below full scale and they are particularly sensitive to rounded corners, guide vanes and railings that set where flow separates.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests\" is correct?","options":["模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。","公開資料顯示本橋的風洞試驗由加拿大邊界層風洞實驗室與丹麥 FORCE Technology 參與。","只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。"],"optionsEn":["If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter.","Public records show the bridge's wind-tunnel testing involved the Boundary Layer Wind Tunnel Laboratory in Canada and FORCE Technology in Denmark.","One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開資料顯示本橋的風洞試驗由加拿大邊界層風洞實驗室與丹麥 FORCE Technology 參與。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Public records show the bridge's wind-tunnel testing involved the Boundary Layer Wind Tunnel Laboratory in Canada and FORCE Technology in Denmark. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b004-v13-26","title":"風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應：定量估算","titleEn":"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面模型雷諾數」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Section-model Reynolds number” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：雷諾數 Re = U·B/ν。實橋 U = 70 m/s、B = 45 m、ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s：Re ≈ 2.1×10⁸；1:50 模型 B = 0.9 m、試驗風速 10 m/s：Re ≈ 6.0×10⁵，相差約 350 倍。若模型提高到 1:25 且風速 15 m/s，Re ≈ 1.8×10⁶，差距縮為約 117 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Reynolds number Re = U·B/ν. Full scale with U = 70 m/s, B = 45 m and ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s gives Re ≈ 2.1×10⁸; a 1:50 model with B = 0.9 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 6.0×10⁵, about 350 times smaller. A 1:25 model at 15 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.8×10⁶, narrowing the gap to about 117 times. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同風速與不同比例模型下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，確認結果是否隨雷諾數改變；兩個實驗室對相同斷面的顫振臨界風速差異應在事先約定的範圍內，否則須找出原因（模型阻尼、紊流、支撐剛度）。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes across speeds and model scales to see whether results drift with Reynolds number; the flutter onset found by two laboratories for the same section should agree within a pre-agreed band, otherwise identify the cause (model damping, turbulence, support stiffness).","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"雷諾數 Re = U·B/ν。實橋 U = 70 m/s、B = 45 m、ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s：Re ≈ 2.1×10⁸；1:50 模型 B = 0.9 m、試驗風速 10 m/s：Re ≈ 6.0×10⁵，相差約 350 倍。若模型提高到 1:25 且風速 15 m/s，Re ≈ 1.8×10⁶，差距縮為約 117 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Reynolds number Re = U·B/ν. Full scale with U = 70 m/s, B = 45 m and ν = 1.5×10⁻⁵ m²/s gives Re ≈ 2.1×10⁸; a 1:50 model with B = 0.9 m at 10 m/s gives Re ≈ 6.0×10⁵, about 350 times smaller. A 1:25 model at 15 m/s gives Re ≈ 1.8×10⁶, narrowing the gap to about 117 times. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests\", which statement holds?","options":["伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。","橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。","雷諾數 Re = U·B/ν。"],"optionsEn":["An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter.","An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance.","Reynolds number Re = U·B/ν."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雷諾數 Re = U·B/ν。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Reynolds number Re = U·B/ν. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b004-v13-27","title":"風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面模型雷諾數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Section-model Reynolds number” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同風速與不同比例模型下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，確認結果是否隨雷諾數改變；兩個實驗室對相同斷面的顫振臨界風速差異應在事先約定的範圍內，否則須找出原因（模型阻尼、紊流、支撐剛度）。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes across speeds and model scales to see whether results drift with Reynolds number; the flutter onset found by two laboratories for the same section should agree within a pre-agreed band, otherwise identify the cause (model damping, turbulence, support stiffness). Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：風洞合約應要求提交模型頻率與阻尼校核、紊流特性、雷諾數敏感度試驗與原始資料；設計者應指定由獨立驗證單位複核關鍵試驗，並把未能以模型確認的細部列入完工後的監測重點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Wind-tunnel contracts should require model frequency and damping calibration, turbulence characteristics, Reynolds-sensitivity runs and raw data; the designer should have the independent checker review key tests and list details the model could not confirm as monitoring priorities after completion.","failure":"注意干擾：若圓角或欄杆細部對雷諾數敏感而未察覺，模型可能顯示沒有渦振，但實橋在某風速範圍出現明顯振動；單一實驗室的系統誤差也可能讓顫振裕度被高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If a rounded corner or railing detail is Reynolds-sensitive and this goes unnoticed, the model may show no vortex vibration while the real deck vibrates noticeably in some wind range; a single laboratory's systematic error can also overstate flutter margin. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同風速與不同比例模型下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，確認結果是否隨雷諾數改變；兩個實驗室對相同斷面的顫振臨界風速差異應在事先約定的範圍內，否則須找出原因（模型阻尼、紊流、支撐剛度）。","textEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes across speeds and model scales to see whether results drift with Reynolds number; the flutter onset found by two laboratories for the same section should agree within a pre-agreed band, otherwise identify the cause (model damping, turbulence, support stiffness).","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"風洞合約應要求提交模型頻率與阻尼校核、紊流特性、雷諾數敏感度試驗與原始資料；設計者應指定由獨立驗證單位複核關鍵試驗，並把未能以模型確認的細部列入完工後的監測重點。","textEn":"Wind-tunnel contracts should require model frequency and damping calibration, turbulence characteristics, Reynolds-sensitivity runs and raw data; the designer should have the independent checker review key tests and list details the model could not confirm as monitoring priorities after completion.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests\"?","options":["比較不同風速與不同比例模型下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，確認結果是否隨雷諾數改變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。"],"optionsEn":["Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes across speeds and model scales to see whether results drift with Reynolds number.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較不同風速與不同比例模型下的氣動係數與渦振振幅，確認結果是否隨雷諾數改變；兩個實驗室對相同斷面的顫振臨界風速差異應在事先約定的範圍內，否則須找出原因（模型阻尼、紊流、支撐剛度）。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare aerodynamic coefficients and vortex amplitudes across speeds and model scales to see whether results drift with Reynolds number; the flutter onset found by two laboratories for the same section should agree within a pre-agreed band, otherwise identify the cause (model damping, turbulence, support stiffness). Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b004-v13-28","title":"風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應：失效診斷","titleEn":"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面模型雷諾數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Section-model Reynolds number” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若圓角或欄杆細部對雷諾數敏感而未察覺，模型可能顯示沒有渦振，但實橋在某風速範圍出現明顯振動；單一實驗室的系統誤差也可能讓顫振裕度被高估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If a rounded corner or railing detail is Reynolds-sensitive and this goes unnoticed, the model may show no vortex vibration while the real deck vibrates noticeably in some wind range; a single laboratory's systematic error can also overstate flutter margin. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此試驗計畫常以不同風速重複試驗觀察趨勢，必要時用加大比例的局部模型或計算流體力學輔助判讀，並以多個實驗室交叉比對結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Test programmes therefore repeat runs at several speeds to watch trends, use larger-scale partial models or computational fluid dynamics where needed, and cross-check results between laboratories.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若圓角或欄杆細部對雷諾數敏感而未察覺，模型可能顯示沒有渦振，但實橋在某風速範圍出現明顯振動；單一實驗室的系統誤差也可能讓顫振裕度被高估。","textEn":"If a rounded corner or railing detail is Reynolds-sensitive and this goes unnoticed, the model may show no vortex vibration while the real deck vibrates noticeably in some wind range; a single laboratory's systematic error can also overstate flutter margin.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「風洞試驗的相似性與雷諾數效應」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Similarity and Reynolds effects in wind-tunnel tests\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若圓角或欄杆細部對雷諾數敏感而未察覺，模型可能顯示沒有渦振，但實橋在某風速範圍出現明顯振動；單一實驗室的系統誤差也可能讓顫振裕度被高估。","只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If a rounded corner or railing detail is Reynolds-sensitive and this goes unnoticed, the model may show no vortex vibration while the real deck vibrates noticeably in some wind range.","One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若圓角或欄杆細部對雷諾數敏感而未察覺，模型可能顯示沒有渦振，但實橋在某風速範圍出現明顯振動；單一實驗室的系統誤差也可能讓顫振裕度被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If a rounded corner or railing detail is Reynolds-sensitive and this goes unnoticed, the model may show no vortex vibration while the real deck vibrates noticeably in some wind range; a single laboratory's systematic error can also overstate flutter margin. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b004-v13-29","title":"以振動頻率驗證吊索力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「吊索振動法張力」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hanger tension by vibration” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"橋面節塊掛上吊索後，每根吊索的實際張力決定了荷重是否如設計般分配到主纜，也影響索夾滑移與局部疲勞。直接在每根吊索裝荷重計成本高，因此常用振動法：量測吊索自然頻率，由弦公式反算張力。較短或較粗的吊索彎曲勁度不可忽略，端部錨頭與索夾的邊界條件也會改變頻率，需以修正公式或有限元素模型校正，並以少數裝有荷重計或千斤頂的吊索作為標定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「吊索振動法張力」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Once deck blocks hang from the hangers, the actual force in each hanger shows whether load reaches the cables as designed, and it also affects cable-band slip and local fatigue. Fitting a load cell to every hanger is costly, so the vibration method is common: measure the hanger's natural frequencies and back-calculate tension from the string formula. Bending stiffness of short or stout hangers cannot be ignored and end sockets and cable bands change the boundary conditions, so a corrected formula or finite-element model is calibrated against a few hangers fitted with load cells or jacks. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Hanger tension by vibration” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：弦公式 T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: String formula T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n².","failure":"常見誤解：「只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「吊索振動法張力」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Hanger tension by vibration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-29-k1","title":"以振動頻率驗證吊索力","titleEn":"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency","text":"橋面節塊掛上吊索後，每根吊索的實際張力決定了荷重是否如設計般分配到主纜，也影響索夾滑移與局部疲勞。直接在每根吊索裝荷重計成本高，因此常用振動法：量測吊索自然頻率，由弦公式反算張力。","textEn":"Once deck blocks hang from the hangers, the actual force in each hanger shows whether load reaches the cables as designed, and it also affects cable-band slip and local fatigue. Fitting a load cell to every hanger is costly, so the vibration method is common: measure the hanger's natural frequencies and back-calculate tension from the string formula.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「以振動頻率驗證吊索力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency\" is correct?","options":["只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。","主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。","橋面節塊掛上吊索後，每根吊索的實際張力決定了荷重是否如設計般分配到主纜，也影響索夾滑移與局部疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely.","The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.","Once deck blocks hang from the hangers, the actual force in each hanger shows whether load reaches the cables as designed, and it also affects cable-band slip and local fatigue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橋面節塊掛上吊索後，每根吊索的實際張力決定了荷重是否如設計般分配到主纜，也影響索夾滑移與局部疲勞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Once deck blocks hang from the hangers, the actual force in each hanger shows whether load reaches the cables as designed, and it also affects cable-band slip and local fatigue. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b004-v13-30","title":"以振動頻率驗證吊索力：定量估算","titleEn":"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吊索振動法張力」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hanger tension by vibration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：弦公式 T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n²。取 m = 60 kg/m、L = 100 m、第一模態 f₁ = 0.9 Hz：T = 4×60×100²×0.9² ≈ 1.94 MN。頻率量測誤差 2% 會造成張力誤差約 1.02² − 1 ≈ 4%，因此頻率解析度與有效長度的判定都很關鍵。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: String formula T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n². With m = 60 kg/m, L = 100 m and first-mode f₁ = 0.9 Hz: T = 4×60×100²×0.9² ≈ 1.94 MN. A 2% frequency error gives a tension error of about 1.02² − 1 ≈ 4%, so frequency resolution and the effective length both matter. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在每根吊索上以加速度計記錄環境振動數分鐘，取多個模態頻率以線性回歸 f_n/n 與 n 的關係分離彎曲勁度影響；結果與施工階段分析的預測吊索力比較，偏差超過約定門檻（例如 ±10%）的吊索列入調整或複測清單。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record ambient vibration on every hanger for several minutes with an accelerometer, use several modal frequencies and regress f_n/n against n to separate bending-stiffness effects; compare with forces predicted by the construction-stage analysis and put hangers deviating beyond an agreed threshold, such as ±10%, on an adjustment or re-test list.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"弦公式 T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n²。取 m = 60 kg/m、L = 100 m、第一模態 f₁ = 0.9 Hz：T = 4×60×100²×0.9² ≈ 1.94 MN。頻率量測誤差 2% 會造成張力誤差約 1.02² − 1 ≈ 4%，因此頻率解析度與有效長度的判定都很關鍵。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"String formula T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n². With m = 60 kg/m, L = 100 m and first-mode f₁ = 0.9 Hz: T = 4×60×100²×0.9² ≈ 1.94 MN. A 2% frequency error gives a tension error of about 1.02² − 1 ≈ 4%, so frequency resolution and the effective length both matter. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「以振動頻率驗證吊索力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency\", which statement holds?","options":["弦公式 T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n²。","塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。","只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。"],"optionsEn":["String formula T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n².","Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper.","As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"弦公式 T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"String formula T = 4·m·L²·f_n²/n². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b004-v13-31","title":"以振動頻率驗證吊索力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吊索振動法張力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hanger tension by vibration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在每根吊索上以加速度計記錄環境振動數分鐘，取多個模態頻率以線性回歸 f_n/n 與 n 的關係分離彎曲勁度影響；結果與施工階段分析的預測吊索力比較，偏差超過約定門檻（例如 ±10%）的吊索列入調整或複測清單。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record ambient vibration on every hanger for several minutes with an accelerometer, use several modal frequencies and regress f_n/n against n to separate bending-stiffness effects; compare with forces predicted by the construction-stage analysis and put hangers deviating beyond an agreed threshold, such as ±10%, on an adjustment or re-test list. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：吊索力量測要在溫度穩定、無施工荷重移動的時段進行，記錄溫度與當時的施工狀態；完工時的全橋吊索力表應納入交接文件，作為營運期每次檢測的比較基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure hanger forces when temperature is steady and no construction loads are moving, logging temperature and construction state; include the full set of completion hanger forces in the handover documents as the baseline for every later inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：若忽略彎曲勁度或錯用有效長度，短吊索的張力會被系統性高估或低估，導致錯誤調整；吊索力分配不均會讓個別索夾承受過大的下滑力，長期可能出現索夾滑移與防護層破損。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring bending stiffness or using the wrong effective length systematically misjudges short-hanger tension and leads to wrong adjustments; uneven hanger forces load individual cable bands with excessive sliding force, which over time can cause band slip and damage to the protection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在每根吊索上以加速度計記錄環境振動數分鐘，取多個模態頻率以線性回歸 f_n/n 與 n 的關係分離彎曲勁度影響；結果與施工階段分析的預測吊索力比較，偏差超過約定門檻（例如 ±10%）的吊索列入調整或複測清單。","textEn":"Record ambient vibration on every hanger for several minutes with an accelerometer, use several modal frequencies and regress f_n/n against n to separate bending-stiffness effects; compare with forces predicted by the construction-stage analysis and put hangers deviating beyond an agreed threshold, such as ±10%, on an adjustment or re-test list.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"吊索力量測要在溫度穩定、無施工荷重移動的時段進行，記錄溫度與當時的施工狀態；完工時的全橋吊索力表應納入交接文件，作為營運期每次檢測的比較基準。","textEn":"Measure hanger forces when temperature is steady and no construction loads are moving, logging temperature and construction state; include the full set of completion hanger forces in the handover documents as the baseline for every later inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「以振動頻率驗證吊索力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在每根吊索上以加速度計記錄環境振動數分鐘，取多個模態頻率以線性回歸 f_n/n 與 n 的關係分離彎曲勁度影響。","沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Record ambient vibration on every hanger for several minutes with an accelerometer, use several modal frequencies and regress f_n/n against n to separate bending-stiffness effects.","A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在每根吊索上以加速度計記錄環境振動數分鐘，取多個模態頻率以線性回歸 f_n/n 與 n 的關係分離彎曲勁度影響；結果與施工階段分析的預測吊索力比較，偏差超過約定門檻（例如 ±10%）的吊索列入調整或複測清單。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record ambient vibration on every hanger for several minutes with an accelerometer, use several modal frequencies and regress f_n/n against n to separate bending-stiffness effects; compare with forces predicted by the construction-stage analysis and put hangers deviating beyond an agreed threshold, such as ±10%, on an adjustment or re-test list. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b004-v13-32","title":"以振動頻率驗證吊索力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吊索振動法張力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hanger tension by vibration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若忽略彎曲勁度或錯用有效長度，短吊索的張力會被系統性高估或低估，導致錯誤調整；吊索力分配不均會讓個別索夾承受過大的下滑力，長期可能出現索夾滑移與防護層破損。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring bending stiffness or using the wrong effective length systematically misjudges short-hanger tension and leads to wrong adjustments; uneven hanger forces load individual cable bands with excessive sliding force, which over time can cause band slip and damage to the protection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：較短或較粗的吊索彎曲勁度不可忽略，端部錨頭與索夾的邊界條件也會改變頻率，需以修正公式或有限元素模型校正，並以少數裝有荷重計或千斤頂的吊索作為標定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bending stiffness of short or stout hangers cannot be ignored and end sockets and cable bands change the boundary conditions, so a corrected formula or finite-element model is calibrated against a few hangers fitted with load cells or jacks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要量到吊索的一個頻率，就能精確算出張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One measured hanger frequency is enough to compute tension precisely.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若忽略彎曲勁度或錯用有效長度，短吊索的張力會被系統性高估或低估，導致錯誤調整；吊索力分配不均會讓個別索夾承受過大的下滑力，長期可能出現索夾滑移與防護層破損。","textEn":"Ignoring bending stiffness or using the wrong effective length systematically misjudges short-hanger tension and leads to wrong adjustments; uneven hanger forces load individual cable bands with excessive sliding force, which over time can cause band slip and damage to the protection.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「以振動頻率驗證吊索力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Verifying hanger forces by vibration frequency\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。","若忽略彎曲勁度或錯用有效長度，短吊索的張力會被系統性高估或低估，導致錯誤調整；吊索力分配不均會讓個別索夾承受過大的下滑力，長期可能出現索夾滑移與防護層破損。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.","Ignoring bending stiffness or using the wrong effective length systematically misjudges short-hanger tension and leads to wrong adjustments."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若忽略彎曲勁度或錯用有效長度，短吊索的張力會被系統性高估或低估，導致錯誤調整；吊索力分配不均會讓個別索夾承受過大的下滑力，長期可能出現索夾滑移與防護層破損。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring bending stiffness or using the wrong effective length systematically misjudges short-hanger tension and leads to wrong adjustments; uneven hanger forces load individual cable bands with excessive sliding force, which over time can cause band slip and damage to the protection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b004-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部」與「伸縮縫行程與營運交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck\" and \"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b004-v13-33","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「鋼橋面板肋焊道」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel deck rib welds” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"懸索橋的鋼箱梁頂板直接承受輪壓，縱肋與頂板、縱肋與橫隔板的焊接處在每次重車通過時都經歷局部應力循環。這類疲勞以局部彎曲為主，與整體主纜受力關係不大，因此主跨長度不會減輕它；交通量越大、重車比例越高，焊道累積的損傷越快。設計上可以加厚頂板、改善縱肋與橫隔板的切口形狀、規定全滲透或高熔深焊接，並在鋪面上選擇較高勁度的材料分散輪壓。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼橋面板肋焊道」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The top plate of a suspension bridge's steel box carries wheel loads directly, and the welds between ribs and deck plate and between ribs and diaphragms go through local stress cycles with every heavy vehicle. This fatigue is dominated by local bending and has little to do with global cable forces, so a long main span does nothing to relieve it; the more traffic and the higher the share of heavy trucks, the faster damage accumulates at the welds. Designers can thicken the deck plate, improve rib-to-diaphragm cut-out shapes, specify full or deep-penetration welds, and choose stiffer surfacing that spreads wheel loads. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Steel deck rib welds” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：局部彎曲應力約與頂板厚度平方成反比：t 由 14 mm 增為 18 mm，應力比 (14/18)² ≈ 0.605。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Local bending stress is roughly inversely proportional to the square of deck-plate thickness: going from 14 mm to 18 mm gives a stress ratio of (14/18)² ≈ 0.605.","failure":"常見誤解：「主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼橋面板肋焊道」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Steel deck rib welds”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-33-k1","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部","titleEn":"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck","text":"懸索橋的鋼箱梁頂板直接承受輪壓，縱肋與頂板、縱肋與橫隔板的焊接處在每次重車通過時都經歷局部應力循環。這類疲勞以局部彎曲為主，與整體主纜受力關係不大，因此主跨長度不會減輕它；交通量越大、重車比例越高，焊道累積的損傷越快。","textEn":"The top plate of a suspension bridge's steel box carries wheel loads directly, and the welds between ribs and deck plate and between ribs and diaphragms go through local stress cycles with every heavy vehicle. This fatigue is dominated by local bending and has little to do with global cable forces, so a long main span does nothing to relieve it; the more traffic and the higher the share of heavy trucks, the faster damage accumulates at the welds.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck\" is correct?","options":["懸索橋的鋼箱梁頂板直接承受輪壓，縱肋與頂板、縱肋與橫隔板的焊接處在每次重車通過時都經歷局部應力循環。","主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。","伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。"],"optionsEn":["The top plate of a suspension bridge's steel box carries wheel loads directly, and the welds between ribs and deck plate and between ribs and diaphragms go through local stress cycles with every heavy vehicle.","The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.","An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"懸索橋的鋼箱梁頂板直接承受輪壓，縱肋與頂板、縱肋與橫隔板的焊接處在每次重車通過時都經歷局部應力循環。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The top plate of a suspension bridge's steel box carries wheel loads directly, and the welds between ribs and deck plate and between ribs and diaphragms go through local stress cycles with every heavy vehicle. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b004-v13-34","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部：定量估算","titleEn":"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼橋面板肋焊道」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel deck rib welds” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：局部彎曲應力約與頂板厚度平方成反比：t 由 14 mm 增為 18 mm，應力比 (14/18)² ≈ 0.605。若 S–N 曲線斜率 m = 3，疲勞壽命比 = (1/0.605)³ ≈ 4.5 倍；即同樣交通下，加厚頂板可把焊道壽命延長約 4.5 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Local bending stress is roughly inversely proportional to the square of deck-plate thickness: going from 14 mm to 18 mm gives a stress ratio of (14/18)² ≈ 0.605. With an S–N slope of m = 3, the fatigue-life ratio is (1/0.605)³ ≈ 4.5, so under the same traffic a thicker plate extends weld life by about 4.5 times. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：製造時以超音波或相位陣列檢查縱肋焊道熔深，抽樣切片確認；完工前在代表性位置貼應變計做載重車試驗，量測實際應力範圍與分析比較；營運期以目視、磁粉或渦流檢測定期檢查焊趾與切口。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: During fabrication check rib-weld penetration by ultrasonic or phased-array testing with sample macro-sections; before opening, strain-gauge representative locations and run a test-truck programme to compare measured stress ranges with analysis; in service inspect weld toes and cut-outs periodically by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"局部彎曲應力約與頂板厚度平方成反比：t 由 14 mm 增為 18 mm，應力比 (14/18)² ≈ 0.605。若 S–N 曲線斜率 m = 3，疲勞壽命比 = (1/0.605)³ ≈ 4.5 倍；即同樣交通下，加厚頂板可把焊道壽命延長約 4.5 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Local bending stress is roughly inversely proportional to the square of deck-plate thickness: going from 14 mm to 18 mm gives a stress ratio of (14/18)² ≈ 0.605. With an S–N slope of m = 3, the fatigue-life ratio is (1/0.605)³ ≈ 4.5, so under the same traffic a thicker plate extends weld life by about 4.5 times. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck\", which statement holds?","options":["橋面中間開口會削弱橋梁，因此對抗風一定不利。","局部彎曲應力約與頂板厚度平方成反比：t 由 14 mm 增為 18 mm，應力比 (14/18)² ≈ 0.605。","基礎在地震中滑動就代表設計失敗。"],"optionsEn":["An opening in the middle of the deck weakens the bridge and must be bad for wind resistance.","Local bending stress is roughly inversely proportional to the square of deck-plate thickness: going from 14 mm to 18 mm gives a stress ratio of (14/18)² ≈ 0.605.","If a foundation slides in an earthquake, the design has failed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部彎曲應力約與頂板厚度平方成反比：t 由 14 mm 增為 18 mm，應力比 (14/18)² ≈ 0.605。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Local bending stress is roughly inversely proportional to the square of deck-plate thickness: going from 14 mm to 18 mm gives a stress ratio of (14/18)² ≈ 0.605. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b004-v13-35","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼橋面板肋焊道」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel deck rib welds” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"製造時以超音波或相位陣列檢查縱肋焊道熔深，抽樣切片確認；完工前在代表性位置貼應變計做載重車試驗，量測實際應力範圍與分析比較；營運期以目視、磁粉或渦流檢測定期檢查焊趾與切口。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"During fabrication check rib-weld penetration by ultrasonic or phased-array testing with sample macro-sections; before opening, strain-gauge representative locations and run a test-truck programme to compare measured stress ranges with analysis; in service inspect weld toes and cut-outs periodically by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：鋼橋面焊接程序評定應包含熔深與焊趾形狀要求，並在製造廠建立首件檢查與定期切片制度；交接時提供鋪面材料、交通量假設與疲勞熱點清單，供營運單位規劃檢查週期。","observationEn":"Site practice: Welding procedure qualification for the steel deck should include penetration and toe-profile requirements, with first-article inspection and periodic macro-sections at the fabricator; at handover supply the surfacing materials, traffic assumptions and a fatigue hot-spot list so the operator can plan inspection intervals.","failure":"注意干擾：縱肋與頂板焊根的疲勞裂縫可能向頂板內擴展而不易從箱內看見，最終造成鋪面開裂與滲水；橫隔板切口的裂縫則會延伸到腹板。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fatigue cracks at the rib-to-deck weld root can grow into the deck plate without being visible from inside the box, eventually cracking the surfacing and letting water in; cracks at diaphragm cut-outs can run into the web. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"製造時以超音波或相位陣列檢查縱肋焊道熔深，抽樣切片確認；完工前在代表性位置貼應變計做載重車試驗，量測實際應力範圍與分析比較；營運期以目視、磁粉或渦流檢測定期檢查焊趾與切口。","textEn":"During fabrication check rib-weld penetration by ultrasonic or phased-array testing with sample macro-sections; before opening, strain-gauge representative locations and run a test-truck programme to compare measured stress ranges with analysis; in service inspect weld toes and cut-outs periodically by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"鋼橋面焊接程序評定應包含熔深與焊趾形狀要求，並在製造廠建立首件檢查與定期切片制度；交接時提供鋪面材料、交通量假設與疲勞熱點清單，供營運單位規劃檢查週期。","textEn":"Welding procedure qualification for the steel deck should include penetration and toe-profile requirements, with first-article inspection and periodic macro-sections at the fabricator; at handover supply the surfacing materials, traffic assumptions and a fatigue hot-spot list so the operator can plan inspection intervals.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","索鞍在施工期間固定不動，主纜就會自然平衡。","製造時以超音波或相位陣列檢查縱肋焊道熔深，抽樣切片確認。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Saddles stay fixed during construction and the cables balance themselves.","During fabrication check rib-weld penetration by ultrasonic or phased-array testing with sample macro-sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"製造時以超音波或相位陣列檢查縱肋焊道熔深，抽樣切片確認；完工前在代表性位置貼應變計做載重車試驗，量測實際應力範圍與分析比較；營運期以目視、磁粉或渦流檢測定期檢查焊趾與切口。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"During fabrication check rib-weld penetration by ultrasonic or phased-array testing with sample macro-sections; before opening, strain-gauge representative locations and run a test-truck programme to compare measured stress ranges with analysis; in service inspect weld toes and cut-outs periodically by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b004-v13-36","title":"正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼橋面板肋焊道」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel deck rib welds” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縱肋與頂板焊根的疲勞裂縫可能向頂板內擴展而不易從箱內看見，最終造成鋪面開裂與滲水；橫隔板切口的裂縫則會延伸到腹板。這類問題在多座早期鋼箱梁橋已有案例，修補需封閉車道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fatigue cracks at the rib-to-deck weld root can grow into the deck plate without being visible from inside the box, eventually cracking the surfacing and letting water in; cracks at diaphragm cut-outs can run into the web. Many early steel-box bridges have had such problems, and repairs require lane closures. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計上可以加厚頂板、改善縱肋與橫隔板的切口形狀、規定全滲透或高熔深焊接，並在鋪面上選擇較高勁度的材料分散輪壓。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Designers can thicken the deck plate, improve rib-to-diaphragm cut-out shapes, specify full or deep-penetration welds, and choose stiffer surfacing that spreads wheel loads.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主跨越長，橋面承受的車輛荷重比例越小，所以鋼橋面不會疲勞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The longer the span, the smaller the share of vehicle load, so the steel deck cannot suffer fatigue.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縱肋與頂板焊根的疲勞裂縫可能向頂板內擴展而不易從箱內看見，最終造成鋪面開裂與滲水；橫隔板切口的裂縫則會延伸到腹板。這類問題在多座早期鋼箱梁橋已有案例，修補需封閉車道。","textEn":"Fatigue cracks at the rib-to-deck weld root can grow into the deck plate without being visible from inside the box, eventually cracking the surfacing and letting water in; cracks at diaphragm cut-outs can run into the web. Many early steel-box bridges have had such problems, and repairs require lane closures.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「正交異性鋼橋面的疲勞細部」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fatigue details of the orthotropic steel deck\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縱肋與頂板焊根的疲勞裂縫可能向頂板內擴展而不易從箱內看見，最終造成鋪面開裂與滲水；橫隔板切口的裂縫則會延伸到腹板。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。"],"optionsEn":["Fatigue cracks at the rib-to-deck weld root can grow into the deck plate without being visible from inside the box, eventually cracking the surfacing and letting water in.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縱肋與頂板焊根的疲勞裂縫可能向頂板內擴展而不易從箱內看見，最終造成鋪面開裂與滲水；橫隔板切口的裂縫則會延伸到腹板。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fatigue cracks at the rib-to-deck weld root can grow into the deck plate without being visible from inside the box, eventually cracking the surfacing and letting water in; cracks at diaphragm cut-outs can run into the web. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b004-v13-37","title":"伸縮縫行程與營運交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「主跨伸縮縫行程」如何影響1915 恰納卡萊大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Main-span joint travel” governs force, deformation or durability in “1915 Canakkale Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"超長跨懸索橋的橋面在溫度、活載、風與地震下會沿縱向移動，伸縮縫與支承要容納這些位移而不卡死。公開資料顯示本橋伸縮縫由 MAURER 供應。除了最大行程，長期累積的滑移距離與速度決定滑動元件與密封的磨耗；車流越大，交通引起的微小往復位移越多。營運單位交接時必須取得設計行程、預設位置與溫度的關係，以及監測位移的基準，才能判斷日後的位移是正常溫度反應還是異常。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「主跨伸縮縫行程」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The deck of a super-long suspension bridge moves longitudinally under temperature, live load, wind and earthquake, and expansion joints and bearings must absorb this without locking. Public records show the expansion joints were supplied by MAURER. Beyond maximum travel, long-term accumulated sliding distance and speed govern wear of sliding elements and seals; heavier traffic means more small reciprocating movements. At handover the operator must receive the design travel, the relationship between preset position and temperature, and a baseline for monitored displacement, to judge whether later movement is a normal thermal response or an anomaly. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Main-span joint travel” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","failure":"常見誤解：「伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「主跨伸縮縫行程」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Main-span joint travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-37-k1","title":"伸縮縫行程與營運交接","titleEn":"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover","text":"超長跨懸索橋的橋面在溫度、活載、風與地震下會沿縱向移動，伸縮縫與支承要容納這些位移而不卡死。公開資料顯示本橋伸縮縫由 MAURER 供應。","textEn":"The deck of a super-long suspension bridge moves longitudinally under temperature, live load, wind and earthquake, and expansion joints and bearings must absorb this without locking. Public records show the expansion joints were supplied by MAURER.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「伸縮縫行程與營運交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover\" is correct?","options":["伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。","超長跨懸索橋的橋面在溫度、活載、風與地震下會沿縱向移動，伸縮縫與支承要容納這些位移而不卡死。","塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。"],"optionsEn":["An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter.","The deck of a super-long suspension bridge moves longitudinally under temperature, live load, wind and earthquake, and expansion joints and bearings must absorb this without locking.","Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"超長跨懸索橋的橋面在溫度、活載、風與地震下會沿縱向移動，伸縮縫與支承要容納這些位移而不卡死。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The deck of a super-long suspension bridge moves longitudinally under temperature, live load, wind and earthquake, and expansion joints and bearings must absorb this without locking. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b004-v13-38","title":"伸縮縫行程與營運交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主跨伸縮縫行程」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Main-span joint travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。設固定點位於跨中、半跨 L = 1,011.5 m、α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /°C、溫差 60 °C：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×1,011.5×60 ≈ 0.73 m。若再加上活載與風造成的縱向位移約 0.5 m，單側伸縮縫需求約 1.2 m 以上。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With the fixed point at mid-span, a half-span L = 1,011.5 m, α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /°C and a 60 °C range: ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×1,011.5×60 ≈ 0.73 m. Adding about 0.5 m of longitudinal movement from live load and wind, each joint needs more than about 1.2 m of travel. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：安裝時依當日橋面溫度設定伸縮縫預設開口，並記錄溫度與開口；營運期以位移計連續記錄伸縮縫開口與橋面溫度，繪出位移—溫度關係，偏離基準趨勢時檢查支承摩擦、卡阻或結構異常。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At installation set the joint opening for the day's deck temperature and record both; in service log joint opening and deck temperature continuously with displacement transducers, plotting displacement against temperature, and investigate bearing friction, binding or structural anomaly when the trend departs from the baseline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。設固定點位於跨中、半跨 L = 1,011.5 m、α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /°C、溫差 60 °C：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×1,011.5×60 ≈ 0.73 m。若再加上活載與風造成的縱向位移約 0.5 m，單側伸縮縫需求約 1.2 m 以上。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With the fixed point at mid-span, a half-span L = 1,011.5 m, α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /°C and a 60 °C range: ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×1,011.5×60 ≈ 0.73 m. Adding about 0.5 m of longitudinal movement from live load and wind, each joint needs more than about 1.2 m of travel. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「伸縮縫行程與營運交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover\", which statement holds?","options":["只要鋼絲抗拉強度夠高，其他性能指標都不重要。","沉箱很重，所以漂浮時一定很穩定，不需要穩性計算。","溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。"],"optionsEn":["As long as tensile strength is high enough, the wire's other properties do not matter.","A caisson is so heavy that it is always stable afloat and needs no stability check.","Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度位移 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Thermal movement ΔL = α·L·ΔT. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b004-v13-39","title":"伸縮縫行程與營運交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主跨伸縮縫行程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Main-span joint travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"安裝時依當日橋面溫度設定伸縮縫預設開口，並記錄溫度與開口；營運期以位移計連續記錄伸縮縫開口與橋面溫度，繪出位移—溫度關係，偏離基準趨勢時檢查支承摩擦、卡阻或結構異常。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At installation set the joint opening for the day's deck temperature and record both; in service log joint opening and deck temperature continuously with displacement transducers, plotting displacement against temperature, and investigate bearing friction, binding or structural anomaly when the trend departs from the baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含伸縮縫與支承的設計行程、安裝溫度與開口紀錄、累積位移監測方法、耗材更換週期與備品清單；營運單位與原設計者應約定異常位移的通報與評估流程。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents should include design travel of joints and bearings, installation temperature and opening records, the method for monitoring accumulated movement, consumable replacement intervals and spares; the operator and original designer should agree a reporting and assessment procedure for abnormal movement.","failure":"注意干擾：伸縮縫預設位置錯誤或行程不足，極端溫度或地震時可能頂死，產生巨大縱向力傳入塔與錨碇；滑動元件磨耗未及時更換，模數式伸縮縫的中梁可能斷裂並危及行車。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A wrongly preset or undersized joint can close up in extreme temperature or an earthquake, driving large longitudinal forces into towers and anchorages; worn sliding elements left unreplaced can let a modular joint's centre beam break and endanger traffic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝時依當日橋面溫度設定伸縮縫預設開口，並記錄溫度與開口；營運期以位移計連續記錄伸縮縫開口與橋面溫度，繪出位移—溫度關係，偏離基準趨勢時檢查支承摩擦、卡阻或結構異常。","textEn":"At installation set the joint opening for the day's deck temperature and record both; in service log joint opening and deck temperature continuously with displacement transducers, plotting displacement against temperature, and investigate bearing friction, binding or structural anomaly when the trend departs from the baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含伸縮縫與支承的設計行程、安裝溫度與開口紀錄、累積位移監測方法、耗材更換週期與備品清單；營運單位與原設計者應約定異常位移的通報與評估流程。","textEn":"Handover documents should include design travel of joints and bearings, installation temperature and opening records, the method for monitoring accumulated movement, consumable replacement intervals and spares; the operator and original designer should agree a reporting and assessment procedure for abnormal movement.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「伸縮縫行程與營運交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover\"?","options":["安裝時依當日橋面溫度設定伸縮縫預設開口，並記錄溫度與開口。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","模型做得越精細，雷諾數差異就不重要。"],"optionsEn":["At installation set the joint opening for the day's deck temperature and record both.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If the model is detailed enough, the Reynolds-number mismatch does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"安裝時依當日橋面溫度設定伸縮縫預設開口，並記錄溫度與開口；營運期以位移計連續記錄伸縮縫開口與橋面溫度，繪出位移—溫度關係，偏離基準趨勢時檢查支承摩擦、卡阻或結構異常。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At installation set the joint opening for the day's deck temperature and record both; in service log joint opening and deck temperature continuously with displacement transducers, plotting displacement against temperature, and investigate bearing friction, binding or structural anomaly when the trend departs from the baseline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b004-v13-40","title":"伸縮縫行程與營運交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"prerequisiteIds":["b004-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主跨伸縮縫行程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Main-span joint travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"伸縮縫預設位置錯誤或行程不足，極端溫度或地震時可能頂死，產生巨大縱向力傳入塔與錨碇；滑動元件磨耗未及時更換，模數式伸縮縫的中梁可能斷裂並危及行車。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A wrongly preset or undersized joint can close up in extreme temperature or an earthquake, driving large longitudinal forces into towers and anchorages; worn sliding elements left unreplaced can let a modular joint's centre beam break and endanger traffic. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：營運單位交接時必須取得設計行程、預設位置與溫度的關係，以及監測位移的基準，才能判斷日後的位移是正常溫度反應還是異常。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At handover the operator must receive the design travel, the relationship between preset position and temperature, and a baseline for monitored displacement, to judge whether later movement is a normal thermal response or an anomaly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「伸縮縫只要容納溫度位移就足夠，不必考慮交通引起的累積滑移。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An expansion joint only needs to absorb thermal movement; accumulated traffic-induced sliding does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b004-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"伸縮縫預設位置錯誤或行程不足，極端溫度或地震時可能頂死，產生巨大縱向力傳入塔與錨碇；滑動元件磨耗未及時更換，模數式伸縮縫的中梁可能斷裂並危及行車。","textEn":"A wrongly preset or undersized joint can close up in extreme temperature or an earthquake, driving large longitudinal forces into towers and anchorages; worn sliding elements left unreplaced can let a modular joint's centre beam break and endanger traffic.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]},{"id":"b004-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「伸縮縫行程與營運交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Expansion-joint travel and operational handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","伸縮縫預設位置錯誤或行程不足，極端溫度或地震時可能頂死，產生巨大縱向力傳入塔與錨碇；滑動元件磨耗未及時更換，模數式伸縮縫的中梁可能斷裂並危及行車。","塔越高越好，因為主纜張力一定會跟著變小，整座橋就越省。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A wrongly preset or undersized joint can close up in extreme temperature or an earthquake, driving large longitudinal forces into towers and anchorages.","Taller towers are always better because lower cable tension makes the whole bridge cheaper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"伸縮縫預設位置錯誤或行程不足，極端溫度或地震時可能頂死，產生巨大縱向力傳入塔與錨碇；滑動元件磨耗未及時更換，模數式伸縮縫的中梁可能斷裂並危及行車。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A wrongly preset or undersized joint can close up in extreme temperature or an earthquake, driving large longitudinal forces into towers and anchorages; worn sliding elements left unreplaced can let a modular joint's centre beam break and endanger traffic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-kgm-canakkale-project","v13s-canakkale-official-timeline","v13s-canakkale-chronicle-04","v13s-cowi-canakkale-news","v13s-structurae-canakkale"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
